8
00:00:25,965 --> 00:00:27,134
Neapolitan Tteokfia.

9
00:00:27,135 --> 00:00:32,035
(The head chef is Lee Young Ji.)

10
00:00:32,335 --> 00:00:34,675
(And they...)

11
00:00:34,975 --> 00:00:37,215
(The crossroads of space and Earth)

12
00:00:37,575 --> 00:00:41,185
(They head to Goheung.)

13
00:00:41,345 --> 00:00:42,345
(Honesty!)

14
00:00:42,345 --> 00:00:43,345
(Humility!)

15
00:00:43,346 --> 00:00:44,814
(One, two, three)

16
00:00:44,815 --> 00:00:47,585
(Ahk!)

17
00:00:47,955 --> 00:00:49,085
(Wait, it's not cut.)

18
00:00:49,585 --> 00:00:54,194
(A bad omen from the start. What lies ahead for Space Rice Cake?)

19
00:00:54,195 --> 00:00:55,964
- Can we go inside and take a look?
- Yes. It's the only restaurant...

20
00:00:55,965 --> 00:00:57,265
- Gosh. What do we do?
- You can go in through that door.

21
00:00:57,365 --> 00:00:59,335
This place has the old-school restaurant vibe.

22
00:00:59,395 --> 00:01:00,904
- Seriously...
- It really does.

23
00:01:00,905 --> 00:01:02,135
- Oh, my gosh.
- Why?

24
00:01:02,535 --> 00:01:04,734
- It's so pretty.
- It's really nice.

25
00:01:04,735 --> 00:01:07,305
Tteokbokki with an ocean view!

26
00:01:07,505 --> 00:01:09,375
- The kitchen is large.
- It's so nice.

27
00:01:10,005 --> 00:01:12,315
(Let us show you around the first Earth location of Space Rice Cake.)

28
00:01:13,145 --> 00:01:14,915
- My, this place is so nice.
- Look at this.

29
00:01:15,085 --> 00:01:16,114
This is insanely beautiful.

30
00:01:16,115 --> 00:01:20,184
(The main kitchen where tasty dishes will be created)

31
00:01:20,185 --> 00:01:21,524
- It's nice.
- Mimi, it's so nice.

32
00:01:21,525 --> 00:01:22,525
It's awesome.

33
00:01:22,526 --> 00:01:24,425
- It's really beautiful.
- There's a stove here.

34
00:01:24,525 --> 00:01:26,324
Let's say "tteokbokki with an ocean view." Ready, go.

35
00:01:26,325 --> 00:01:28,995
- Tteokbokki with an ocean view!
- Tteokbokki with an ocean view!

36
00:01:30,335 --> 00:01:36,464
(The refreshing ocean view from the stove)

37
00:01:36,465 --> 00:01:38,005
Am I bossy? Mimi.

38
00:01:38,135 --> 00:01:42,145
(Even though they bicker from time to time...)

39
00:01:43,745 --> 00:01:47,044
(The deeply bonded chefs will showcase their skills here.)

40
00:01:47,045 --> 00:01:48,045
- It's amazing.
- Indeed.

41
00:01:48,046 --> 00:01:49,415
- This is where we make desserts.
- Right.

42
00:01:49,545 --> 00:01:50,585
This is where we make desserts.

43
00:01:50,985 --> 00:01:53,855
(Next to the main kitchen...)

44
00:01:54,385 --> 00:01:56,655
(Sub-kitchen)

45
00:01:58,525 --> 00:02:01,865
(Sweet desserts will be made here.)

46
00:02:02,095 --> 00:02:03,865
Look at these plates. Mimi likes dishware.

47
00:02:04,695 --> 00:02:06,264
- They're cute.
- We have plates here.

48
00:02:06,265 --> 00:02:07,905
They have Torong on them.

49
00:02:08,035 --> 00:02:10,374
- It says, "Hey, Torong."
- This is where...

50
00:02:10,375 --> 00:02:11,934
Eun Ji and Yu Jin will work busily.

51
00:02:11,935 --> 00:02:13,335
This is a bit too low for me.

52
00:02:14,245 --> 00:02:15,774
- Hold on.
- On top of that, more importantly,

53
00:02:15,775 --> 00:02:17,114
the floor is sloped here.

54
00:02:17,115 --> 00:02:18,774
- It's high enough for me.
- It's easy to move around here.

55
00:02:18,775 --> 00:02:20,814
It's perfect for me.

56
00:02:20,815 --> 00:02:23,215
- It's because Yu Jin is tall.
- Is it too low for her?

57
00:02:23,615 --> 00:02:25,585
- Did you see this machine here?
- This is driving me crazy.

58
00:02:25,755 --> 00:02:27,424
A machine? Oh, I guess we're making our own rice cake.

59
00:02:27,425 --> 00:02:29,125
- Exactly. Look at this.
- We're making our own rice cake.

60
00:02:29,855 --> 00:02:30,954
I guess we're making our own rice cake.

61
00:02:30,955 --> 00:02:32,595
- I suppose we are. I'm worried.
- What is this?

62
00:02:33,125 --> 00:02:34,765
Look at this, Young Ji.

63
00:02:35,165 --> 00:02:36,264
Hold on a second. Head Chef.

64
00:02:36,265 --> 00:02:38,234
- I'm so shocked right now.
- I see.

65
00:02:38,235 --> 00:02:39,494
Nobody told us we'd have to make rice cake.

66
00:02:39,495 --> 00:02:41,405
Think about it. If we make our own rice cake here,

67
00:02:41,565 --> 00:02:44,175
we are going to... I'm not joking.

68
00:02:44,475 --> 00:02:45,505
We are going to...

69
00:02:46,175 --> 00:02:47,605
- get wiped out.
- We'll have to...

70
00:02:48,175 --> 00:02:49,274
We'll have to wake up at 2am.

71
00:02:49,275 --> 00:02:50,774
Actually, we weren't planning on bringing the machine.

72
00:02:50,775 --> 00:02:52,814
We did it because Young Ji said she wanted to make rice cake.

73
00:02:52,815 --> 00:02:54,514
- What are you talking about?
- Come on, Chef Lee.

74
00:02:54,515 --> 00:02:56,044
- What are you talking about?
- I mean...

75
00:02:56,045 --> 00:02:57,854
- Chef Lee.
- You said you wanted to use...

76
00:02:57,855 --> 00:02:59,114
freshly made rice cake for your tteokbokki.

77
00:02:59,115 --> 00:03:01,085
- That's why we brought the machine.
- Chef Lee.

78
00:03:01,185 --> 00:03:03,724
(By any chance, do we have a machine for garaetteok?)

79
00:03:03,725 --> 00:03:05,054
(As Chef Lee made an unexpected request...)

80
00:03:05,055 --> 00:03:06,324
(I used freshly made rice cake during the cook-off,)

81
00:03:06,325 --> 00:03:07,664
(and I realised it yields the best results.)

82
00:03:07,665 --> 00:03:09,064
(- Freshly made ones are the best.
- We'll do our best to pull it off.)

83
00:03:09,065 --> 00:03:12,334
(The staff did their best to make it happen.)

84
00:03:12,335 --> 00:03:13,934
- What should we do?
- How could you make that call...

85
00:03:13,935 --> 00:03:15,805
- all by yourself, Chef Lee?
- How could you do that, Chef Lee?

86
00:03:16,005 --> 00:03:17,834
I didn't know we would have a rice cake machine...

87
00:03:17,835 --> 00:03:20,004
- in Goheung.
- You should have...

88
00:03:20,005 --> 00:03:21,844
asked us first.

89
00:03:21,845 --> 00:03:23,814
- "We'll make our own rice cake."
- Exactly.

90
00:03:23,815 --> 00:03:25,074
- I didn't know they'd bring this.
- But you see,

91
00:03:25,075 --> 00:03:26,444
- she said it in passing.
- That's right.

92
00:03:26,445 --> 00:03:28,344
It was just like saying, "We can make 100,000 dollars..."

93
00:03:28,345 --> 00:03:30,915
"and buy a fancy car with that money."

94
00:03:31,015 --> 00:03:32,254
I never knew they'd actually bring a rice cake machine.

95
00:03:32,255 --> 00:03:33,784
- Let's just take a look at it.
- Also...

96
00:03:33,785 --> 00:03:34,984
- Mind what you say from now on.
- Yes? Go ahead.

97
00:03:34,985 --> 00:03:37,654
Also, we set something up here to help you...

98
00:03:37,655 --> 00:03:39,394
measure the size of the rice cakes.

99
00:03:39,395 --> 00:03:40,564
Is this 175cm long?

100
00:03:40,565 --> 00:03:41,824
- Would you like to pull it out?
- Oh, here it is.

101
00:03:41,825 --> 00:03:43,624
- She said we should do it together.
- This is the regular size.

102
00:03:43,625 --> 00:03:45,335
- One, two, three.
- Two, three.

103
00:03:47,235 --> 00:03:48,465
- One, two, three.
- Two, three.

104
00:03:49,605 --> 00:03:51,235
(Peekaboo)

105
00:03:53,305 --> 00:03:54,644
- Gosh. Hold on a second.
- You wanted rice cakes...

106
00:03:54,645 --> 00:03:55,744
that were as tall as you.

107
00:03:55,745 --> 00:03:57,004
- So we set this up.
- Hold on.

108
00:03:57,005 --> 00:03:58,474
- Hang on.
- You invested too much money...

109
00:03:58,475 --> 00:04:00,374
- in this business, don't you think?
- It's cute.

110
00:04:00,375 --> 00:04:01,514
- When you pull this out...
- That's it.

111
00:04:01,515 --> 00:04:03,114
- That's how far it can slide out.
- Hang on.

112
00:04:03,115 --> 00:04:04,985
- Hold on. Give me a second.
- Hang on.

113
00:04:06,285 --> 00:04:11,554
(They will make good use of it.)

114
00:04:11,555 --> 00:04:12,895
Young Ji, you have nice legs.

115
00:04:13,765 --> 00:04:15,424
- It's an AI-generated image, Mimi.
- Shall we move on?

116
00:04:15,425 --> 00:04:16,795
- Yes, let's take a look over there.
- Let's go.

117
00:04:17,135 --> 00:04:18,365
So this is where we serve food...

118
00:04:18,695 --> 00:04:20,065
Is this a private room?

119
00:04:20,535 --> 00:04:21,804
- Is there a private room too?
- Yes.

120
00:04:21,805 --> 00:04:23,164
- Like a fine dining restaurant.
- What?

121
00:04:23,165 --> 00:04:24,905
- This is a fine dining restaurant.
- Guys, look.

122
00:04:24,975 --> 00:04:28,075
(Down the hall from the kitchen...)

123
00:04:28,705 --> 00:04:31,245
(Main hall)

124
00:04:32,715 --> 00:04:35,714
(4 tables are lined up side by side.)

125
00:04:35,715 --> 00:04:38,155
We can play Guess Who Quiz here. Look at Neapolitan Matfia.

126
00:04:38,485 --> 00:04:39,485
Hello.

127
00:04:39,585 --> 00:04:41,124
- You startled me.
- Did you think he was here?

128
00:04:41,125 --> 00:04:44,494
Young Ji, shouldn't it be your photo instead of his?

129
00:04:44,495 --> 00:04:46,325
(Senior Torong and Manager Kwon?)

130
00:04:48,065 --> 00:04:49,895
(Charming and cosy decorative items fill the room.)

131
00:04:50,765 --> 00:04:52,234
(We wish you great success.)

132
00:04:52,235 --> 00:04:53,665
(Let's aim for opening a 2nd location!)

133
00:04:54,305 --> 00:04:56,365
You're so pretty, just like an idol singer.

134
00:04:56,465 --> 00:04:58,504
- Me? I'm an idol singer.
- Right?

135
00:04:58,505 --> 00:04:59,505
(People share kind words with each other here.)

136
00:05:00,505 --> 00:05:03,675
(It's a place enjoyed by people of all ages and genders.)

137
00:05:05,515 --> 00:05:08,014
(What wonderful memories will be created here?)

138
00:05:08,015 --> 00:05:10,284
May I ask how full you are right now?

139
00:05:10,285 --> 00:05:11,515
Don't worry. We ate a lot.

140
00:05:13,085 --> 00:05:14,825
Guys, we have outdoor tables as well.

141
00:05:16,985 --> 00:05:20,565
(The romantic spot, exclusively at Space Rice Cake)

142
00:05:21,395 --> 00:05:23,025
This place is so beautiful.

143
00:05:23,495 --> 00:05:25,335
This is amazing.

144
00:05:26,495 --> 00:05:27,705
It has a really good vibe.

145
00:05:28,465 --> 00:05:30,005
I really love this vibe.

146
00:05:31,635 --> 00:05:34,375
(Come visit us!)

147
00:05:35,175 --> 00:05:36,204
- The weather is beautiful today.
- It's awesome.

148
00:05:36,205 --> 00:05:37,344
It's so nice here.

149
00:05:37,345 --> 00:05:40,584
Guys, let's make a lot of money and buy this place.

150
00:05:40,585 --> 00:05:42,914
- Exactly. The location is perfect.
- It's really nice.

151
00:05:42,915 --> 00:05:44,854
Many of your senior entertainers sent flowers.

152
00:05:44,855 --> 00:05:45,984
- Who?
- Mr. Lee Kwang Soo!

153
00:05:45,985 --> 00:05:47,454
- Yes.
- Mr. Lee Seo Jin!

154
00:05:47,455 --> 00:05:48,654
- That's amazing.
- What?

155
00:05:48,655 --> 00:05:49,685
- That one is from Torong.
- Which one?

156
00:05:50,225 --> 00:05:51,254
It says, "rice cake..."

157
00:05:51,255 --> 00:05:53,354
- It's from Ms. Youn Yuh Jung.
- Oh, my.

158
00:05:53,355 --> 00:05:55,464
Those are from the cast of "Kang's Kitchen."

159
00:05:55,465 --> 00:05:57,734
Most of them are the cast of old restaurant shows...

160
00:05:57,735 --> 00:06:00,094
- produced by egg is coming.
- That's right.

161
00:06:00,095 --> 00:06:02,364
- They're not imposters, right?
- I think you borrowed their names.

162
00:06:02,365 --> 00:06:04,234
- Exactly. You borrowed their names.
- Are they imposters?

163
00:06:04,235 --> 00:06:05,704
I'm sure Ms. Youn Yuh Jung has no idea...

164
00:06:05,705 --> 00:06:06,935
(Let's move on to the next part of our ceremony.)

165
00:06:07,105 --> 00:06:09,844
- We prepared a small ceremony...
- A traditional ritual?

166
00:06:09,845 --> 00:06:11,715
- to wish for good luck.
- Look at the pig.

167
00:06:12,015 --> 00:06:14,815
How about each of you makes a wish before we open the restaurant?

168
00:06:15,345 --> 00:06:17,614
- She's bowing right away.
- Young Ji, wait. Come back here.

169
00:06:17,615 --> 00:06:20,625
- Young Ji, come back here.
- You should say your wish out loud.

170
00:06:21,055 --> 00:06:23,354
Young Ji, it's not like we have 600 cameras around us.

171
00:06:23,355 --> 00:06:24,495
(Start over again.)

172
00:06:24,755 --> 00:06:26,695
- Mimi, you go first.
- You can call this a main event.

173
00:06:27,925 --> 00:06:29,894
I wish for the good health of everyone here.

174
00:06:29,895 --> 00:06:32,465
I hope nobody gets hurt or slips and falls.

175
00:06:33,035 --> 00:06:34,964
- And I hope we never fight.
- "I hope we never fight."

176
00:06:34,965 --> 00:06:37,235
I hope we fight and go viral with ten million views.

177
00:06:38,675 --> 00:06:40,404
She must be Buddhist.

178
00:06:40,405 --> 00:06:41,745
- Is this how Buddhists bow?
- Yes.

179
00:06:43,105 --> 00:06:44,114
(Next up is Yu Jin.)

180
00:06:44,115 --> 00:06:46,374
- Make a wish with all your heart.
- With sincerity.

181
00:06:46,375 --> 00:06:48,084
- Make sure of it.
- I hope I don't get hurt...

182
00:06:48,085 --> 00:06:49,784
using a knife in the kitchen.

183
00:06:49,785 --> 00:06:52,484
- I hope the girls never fight.
- We all wish for the same thing.

184
00:06:52,485 --> 00:06:54,925
I also hope my cuteness shines through.

185
00:06:55,325 --> 00:06:58,195
Can't you make a wish for the whole team too?

186
00:06:58,595 --> 00:07:01,265
- She wants her cuteness to shine.
- What does she mean by that?

187
00:07:01,425 --> 00:07:02,764
Next up is Eun Ji, who recently wrapped up her radio show.

188
00:07:02,765 --> 00:07:04,135
She must feel liberated.

189
00:07:04,365 --> 00:07:05,465
- Finally...
- She claims to be human arginine.

190
00:07:06,035 --> 00:07:07,094
Human arginine.

191
00:07:07,095 --> 00:07:09,205
We're opening up a restaurant.

192
00:07:10,405 --> 00:07:11,475
I'm so afraid.

193
00:07:12,035 --> 00:07:15,075
- I'm so afraid too.
- Please help us.

194
00:07:16,475 --> 00:07:19,414
(Please grant us courage.)

195
00:07:19,415 --> 00:07:21,384
- Honestly, - This is a traditional ritual.

196
00:07:21,385 --> 00:07:24,084
this restaurant is so nice that I want to invite my friends.

197
00:07:24,085 --> 00:07:25,954
- I agree.
- It'd be nice if you do.

198
00:07:25,955 --> 00:07:28,154
- Invite some of your friends.
- Who would come all the way here?

199
00:07:28,155 --> 00:07:29,425
(It's a 10-hour round trip from Seoul.)

200
00:07:29,685 --> 00:07:31,955
All the members of "Earth Arcade..."

201
00:07:32,695 --> 00:07:35,065
If we're going to fight, let's make sure it's caught on camera.

202
00:07:35,165 --> 00:07:37,195
If anyone's pants fall down, it has to be on camera.

203
00:07:37,565 --> 00:07:40,834
Even if we face conflicts, competition, or hardships,

204
00:07:40,835 --> 00:07:42,105
I hope we can get through them.

205
00:07:43,335 --> 00:07:45,975
Head chefs rarely wear sagging pants.

206
00:07:46,835 --> 00:07:48,845
- She's a next-generation chef.
- A next-generation chef.

207
00:07:49,605 --> 00:07:51,014
Why are you eating the apple?

208
00:07:51,015 --> 00:07:53,075
- That will bring bad luck.
- That will bring bad luck.

209
00:07:55,515 --> 00:07:58,614
Young Ji, discuss your every move before you actually make them.

210
00:07:58,615 --> 00:08:01,455
- I suddenly feel anxious.
- About what?

211
00:08:02,685 --> 00:08:03,924
- I'm anxious now.
- What...

212
00:08:03,925 --> 00:08:06,324
What are we going to do after this ceremony?

213
00:08:06,325 --> 00:08:09,324
What is the main ingredient...

214
00:08:09,325 --> 00:08:10,565
- of Young Ji's dish?
- Yes?

215
00:08:10,995 --> 00:08:12,034
- Rice cake.
- Correct.

216
00:08:12,035 --> 00:08:15,065
- You need to learn how to make it.
- Okay.

217
00:08:15,335 --> 00:08:18,335
- Let's gather here after a break.
- I'm already dressed comfortably.

218
00:08:19,875 --> 00:08:22,075
(They're taking a short break.)

219
00:08:22,445 --> 00:08:23,875
(However...)

220
00:08:24,215 --> 00:08:25,445
Hello.

221
00:08:25,975 --> 00:08:27,075
We opened up a restaurant.

222
00:08:27,345 --> 00:08:29,314
We serve tteokbokki.

223
00:08:29,315 --> 00:08:30,385
- We're quite young.
- You serve tteokbokki?

224
00:08:31,085 --> 00:08:32,654
- Hello, sir.
- Hello.

225
00:08:32,655 --> 00:08:34,954
- She's our head chef.
- Hello.

226
00:08:34,955 --> 00:08:36,655
- Please come for tteokbokki.
- I'm the head of the village.

227
00:08:36,855 --> 00:08:38,654
- Oh, I see.
- The head of the village!

228
00:08:38,655 --> 00:08:41,024
- Spread the word, please.
- Let's salute him.

229
00:08:41,025 --> 00:08:43,864
- Honesty! Humility! Ahk!
- Humility! Ahk!

230
00:08:43,865 --> 00:08:44,865
(They pledge allegiance to him right away.)

231
00:08:45,235 --> 00:08:46,434
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

232
00:08:46,435 --> 00:08:48,064
Is "Ahkun" one of the cast members?

233
00:08:48,065 --> 00:08:49,404
- It's actually "ahk."
- Abu Dhabi...

234
00:08:49,405 --> 00:08:52,674
- In Dubai, it means "big brother."
- It's Arabic. "Big brother."

235
00:08:52,675 --> 00:08:53,974
- "Big brother."
- "Big brother."

236
00:08:53,975 --> 00:08:55,974
I'll visit your restaurant with my wife.

237
00:08:55,975 --> 00:08:57,544
- Please do.
- That'd be great, sir.

238
00:08:57,545 --> 00:08:59,515
- We'll have many customers, sir.
- Oh, there's...

239
00:09:00,375 --> 00:09:03,085
(It's time to make rice cake.)

240
00:09:03,285 --> 00:09:05,514
- Watch your head.
- Watch your head, please.

241
00:09:05,515 --> 00:09:08,284
- Hello. Welcome to Space Rice Cake.
- Hello.

242
00:09:08,285 --> 00:09:11,225
- I'll walk you through the process.
- Okay.

243
00:09:11,355 --> 00:09:14,065
- I'll demonstrate it step-by-step.
- Step by step

244
00:09:14,465 --> 00:09:15,525
So we're going to...

245
00:09:15,665 --> 00:09:17,795
(The types of rice cakes they will learn today)

246
00:09:18,595 --> 00:09:21,904
You'll learn how to make garaetteok for Young Ji's dish...

247
00:09:21,905 --> 00:09:23,935
- and jeolpyeon for Mimi's.
- Jeolpyeon.

248
00:09:24,205 --> 00:09:27,175
- It's basically thin garaetteok.
- Right.

249
00:09:27,505 --> 00:09:30,745
The machines we'll be using are the rice grinder behind you...

250
00:09:30,845 --> 00:09:32,214
- Got it. Rice grinder.
- Yes, that one is used...

251
00:09:32,215 --> 00:09:33,644
- to grind rice.
- Yes.

252
00:09:33,645 --> 00:09:35,844
- And this one is a steamer.
- Steamer.

253
00:09:35,845 --> 00:09:37,784
- We use it to steam rice cakes.
- We can make baekseolgi with it.

254
00:09:37,785 --> 00:09:39,184
- This machine is called jebyeonggi.
- Steamer.

255
00:09:39,185 --> 00:09:40,584
It's a rice cake shaper.

256
00:09:40,585 --> 00:09:41,824
We can shape our rice cakes...

257
00:09:41,825 --> 00:09:43,025
- however we want.
- Right.

258
00:09:43,125 --> 00:09:44,154
(Step 1: Soaking the rice)

259
00:09:44,155 --> 00:09:45,324
You have to prepare the rice in advance.

260
00:09:45,325 --> 00:09:47,354
You can just put the rice in water the night before...

261
00:09:47,355 --> 00:09:48,965
- and store it in the fridge.
- I see.

262
00:09:49,065 --> 00:09:50,665
(Step 2: Grinding the rice)

263
00:09:50,965 --> 00:09:53,034
I'll tell you how to use the rice grinder.

264
00:09:53,035 --> 00:09:54,035
- Okay.
- The rice grinder.

265
00:09:54,036 --> 00:09:56,764
The grinding process consists of two stages.

266
00:09:56,765 --> 00:09:59,375
- Add salt first and then water.
- I see.

267
00:09:59,705 --> 00:10:02,304
Add salt equivalent to 1.2 percent of the rice's total weight.

268
00:10:02,305 --> 00:10:03,305
(Add salt equivalent to 1.2 percent of the rice's total weight.)

269
00:10:03,405 --> 00:10:05,815
(Bring the rice that was soaked overnight...)

270
00:10:06,315 --> 00:10:07,884
(and weigh it on the scale.)

271
00:10:07,885 --> 00:10:08,944
Okay.

272
00:10:08,945 --> 00:10:10,585
- You have to multiply the numbers.
- Yes.

273
00:10:11,515 --> 00:10:13,085
Me? I'm not good at math.

274
00:10:13,555 --> 00:10:14,855
- We can do it together.
- Right.

275
00:10:15,525 --> 00:10:16,585
Do any of you guys have a college degree?

276
00:10:16,885 --> 00:10:17,925
No.

277
00:10:18,255 --> 00:10:20,225
- Eun Ji, didn't you go to college?
- I have a college degree.

278
00:10:20,395 --> 00:10:21,425
Then you do the math.

279
00:10:21,865 --> 00:10:23,125
- I should calculate it?
- Yes.

280
00:10:23,225 --> 00:10:25,495
I gave up on math when I was in the sixth grade. What do I do?

281
00:10:25,895 --> 00:10:28,605
- It took you so long to give up.
- Exactly. This is driving me nuts.

282
00:10:28,735 --> 00:10:30,934
- Multiply 6.2...
- Yes.

283
00:10:30,935 --> 00:10:32,005
- by 0.012...
- Yes.

284
00:10:32,505 --> 00:10:34,405
We should add 74.4g of salt.

285
00:10:35,205 --> 00:10:37,304
- We're doing great.
- Can you prep this for me?

286
00:10:37,305 --> 00:10:38,375
(Add salt and mix everything well.)

287
00:10:38,475 --> 00:10:39,515
- One, two, three.
- One, two, three.

288
00:10:40,075 --> 00:10:41,145
Let's pour it.

289
00:10:41,315 --> 00:10:43,385
I think you can just dump it.

290
00:10:44,415 --> 00:10:45,415
(Grinding)

291
00:10:45,416 --> 00:10:46,485
That's fascinating.

292
00:10:47,185 --> 00:10:49,625
- My, that's pretty.
- It's so fascinating.

293
00:10:49,825 --> 00:10:50,854
It looks like shaved ice.

294
00:10:50,855 --> 00:10:52,455
(The rice flour falls just like snow.)

295
00:10:52,925 --> 00:10:54,364
Mimi, she said...

296
00:10:54,365 --> 00:10:55,794
- you should multiply it by 150.
- Got it.

297
00:10:55,795 --> 00:10:56,825
(Calculate the amount of water, add it, and then grind it again.)

298
00:10:56,865 --> 00:10:59,065
(Stir the mixture gently so it doesn't clump together.)

299
00:10:59,535 --> 00:11:01,205
Young Ji looks like...

300
00:11:01,465 --> 00:11:03,764
a Gen Z entrepreneur opening up a restaurant...

301
00:11:03,765 --> 00:11:06,075
- in Sindang-dong.
- A Gen Zer.

302
00:11:06,535 --> 00:11:08,275
- Here we go. One, two, three.
- One, two, three.

303
00:11:09,145 --> 00:11:10,145
Nice.

304
00:11:10,275 --> 00:11:13,215
(Grind the mixture again with the rice grinder.)

305
00:11:13,775 --> 00:11:16,744
(The finely ground rice flour is ready.)

306
00:11:16,745 --> 00:11:18,515
I didn't know that it was this hard to make rice cake.

307
00:11:19,585 --> 00:11:20,585
I guess that's why it's tasty.

308
00:11:20,685 --> 00:11:23,354
Exactly. There's a reason why mills start working at 4am.

309
00:11:23,355 --> 00:11:24,425
- Exactly.
- That's right.

310
00:11:26,495 --> 00:11:28,895
Yu Jin's eyes look soulless. Get that on camera.

311
00:11:29,465 --> 00:11:31,365
(I never looked like that.)

312
00:11:31,635 --> 00:11:33,565
(Step 3: Steaming baekseolgi)

313
00:11:33,595 --> 00:11:35,434
You just have to pour the rice flour into the container,

314
00:11:35,435 --> 00:11:37,305
leaving about 1cm of space at the top.

315
00:11:37,805 --> 00:11:39,375
- It's a lot.
- It smells good.

316
00:11:40,135 --> 00:11:42,405
- It holds such a large amount.
- Exactly.

317
00:11:42,745 --> 00:11:45,375
The center part looks perfect, so leave it as it is.

318
00:11:45,745 --> 00:11:47,215
Just flatten the edges evenly.

319
00:11:48,215 --> 00:11:50,514
- Even - Evenly

320
00:11:50,515 --> 00:11:51,584
(The word triggers her performer instinct.)

321
00:11:51,585 --> 00:11:52,715
- May I dance, Head Chef?
- Sure.

322
00:11:53,215 --> 00:11:55,424
- Even, even - Now or never. Let's dance.

323
00:11:55,425 --> 00:11:57,555
- Even, even - Nice.

324
00:11:57,655 --> 00:11:58,695
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

325
00:11:59,095 --> 00:12:01,694
You have to open this to drain the water...

326
00:12:01,695 --> 00:12:02,895
- Yes.
- in case there's water in there.

327
00:12:04,435 --> 00:12:05,435
My goodness.

328
00:12:06,235 --> 00:12:09,434
I wonder what lies at the edge of the vast ocean

329
00:12:09,435 --> 00:12:12,274
- Right. That's our Eun Ji.
- There must be

330
00:12:12,275 --> 00:12:13,735
(Atlantis Princess appears in Goheung.)

331
00:12:14,135 --> 00:12:15,745
- She's a natural-born performer.
- She never lets us down.

332
00:12:16,875 --> 00:12:18,745
Look at her flexing her cooking show experience.

333
00:12:18,915 --> 00:12:20,075
Perform "Rebel Heart," please.

334
00:12:21,815 --> 00:12:24,584
- We are rebels in our heart - We are rebels in our heart

335
00:12:24,585 --> 00:12:26,815
(They're almost invisible.)

336
00:12:27,015 --> 00:12:28,285
(The original singer is singing her heart out.)

337
00:12:28,585 --> 00:12:29,655
Isn't it hot?

338
00:12:29,685 --> 00:12:31,395
- It's warm.
- It's like a humidifier.

339
00:12:32,455 --> 00:12:34,565
(Young Ji tries the steam therapy as well.)

340
00:12:35,095 --> 00:12:36,925
Please sing "I Am Lee Young Ji" for us.

341
00:12:37,325 --> 00:12:40,334
- I am Lee Young Ji - It just made a noise, right?

342
00:12:40,335 --> 00:12:41,435
I'll turn this off now.

343
00:12:42,165 --> 00:12:44,904
You just have to cover the rice cake with a damp cloth.

344
00:12:44,905 --> 00:12:45,935
(Cover the container with a cloth and steam it for 20 minutes.)

345
00:12:46,205 --> 00:12:48,605
(Cover it facing away from you so the steam doesn't burn you!)

346
00:12:48,875 --> 00:12:50,074
After you cover it, the cloth puffs up...

347
00:12:50,075 --> 00:12:51,274
- You covered it well.
- Yes.

348
00:12:51,275 --> 00:12:52,314
Impressive. Nice.

349
00:12:52,315 --> 00:12:54,174
When it puffs up, set the timer for 20 minutes.

350
00:12:54,175 --> 00:12:55,715
- Set the timer for 20 minutes.
- Bring the timer.

351
00:12:56,015 --> 00:12:58,415
(After 20 minutes, poke it with a chopstick.)

352
00:12:59,015 --> 00:13:01,025
Look at this. It looks so tasty.

353
00:13:01,785 --> 00:13:04,955
(Baekseolgi is done.)

354
00:13:05,195 --> 00:13:07,155
(Step 4: Running the rice cake dough through the machine)

355
00:13:07,455 --> 00:13:10,525
(Here's the thing about the rice cake shaper.)

356
00:13:11,195 --> 00:13:12,665
So this is how it goes in.

357
00:13:14,065 --> 00:13:15,065
Okay.

358
00:13:15,066 --> 00:13:16,435
(Garaetteok)

359
00:13:17,165 --> 00:13:19,175
(Jeolpyeon)

360
00:13:19,705 --> 00:13:22,105
(The extruding nozzles determine the shape of the rice cake.)

361
00:13:22,575 --> 00:13:25,015
It should be rinsed with water as it comes out of the machine.

362
00:13:25,475 --> 00:13:27,315
So you need a basin filled with water.

363
00:13:27,545 --> 00:13:30,644
And place that large rectangular strainer next to it.

364
00:13:30,645 --> 00:13:31,715
(Line the drying strainer with food-safe plastic wrap.)

365
00:13:31,855 --> 00:13:34,455
The next step requires two people.

366
00:13:34,785 --> 00:13:37,854
One person pulls the rice cake out while measuring the length.

367
00:13:37,855 --> 00:13:40,425
The other person stacks the rice cake in the strainer.

368
00:13:41,025 --> 00:13:42,564
- You two can do this together.
- Okay.

369
00:13:42,565 --> 00:13:43,625
Step behind the machine.

370
00:13:43,995 --> 00:13:45,865
- I'll pull and you stack, okay?
- Sure.

371
00:13:46,965 --> 00:13:48,905
(The 1st attempt at using the rice cake shaper)

372
00:13:48,965 --> 00:13:50,365
You didn't cut off the tip.

373
00:13:50,565 --> 00:13:51,675
Oh, no. Young Ji.

374
00:13:53,675 --> 00:13:54,774
(The rice cake is flopping around helplessly.)

375
00:13:54,775 --> 00:13:55,775
Oh, no. Young Ji.

376
00:13:55,775 --> 00:13:56,775
(The rice cake is flopping around helplessly.)

377
00:13:56,975 --> 00:13:58,345
- Young Ji.
- Give me a second, Eun Ji.

378
00:13:58,745 --> 00:14:00,075
Young Ji.

379
00:14:00,445 --> 00:14:04,685
(It's supposed to look pretty as it comes out.)

380
00:14:05,115 --> 00:14:06,185
My goodness. Young Ji.

381
00:14:07,255 --> 00:14:09,555
(String cheese?)

382
00:14:09,685 --> 00:14:11,155
Young Ji, what do we do with this?

383
00:14:12,395 --> 00:14:14,465
(Both Young Ji and the rice cake...)

384
00:14:14,565 --> 00:14:16,525
(are worn out.)

385
00:14:17,095 --> 00:14:18,335
I can't get the hang of it.

386
00:14:20,065 --> 00:14:22,035
- How about I stack it?
- Okay. You do that.

387
00:14:22,935 --> 00:14:23,965
I'm ready.

388
00:14:24,735 --> 00:14:25,835
- Shall we begin?
- Yes.

389
00:14:27,875 --> 00:14:31,005
(Despite her cheerful spirit, she's all over the place from the start.)

390
00:14:31,875 --> 00:14:34,174
- Young Ji. I couldn't do it.
- Eun Ji, put it in the water.

391
00:14:34,175 --> 00:14:35,314
I couldn't put it in the water.

392
00:14:35,315 --> 00:14:36,345
(Crying)

393
00:14:36,545 --> 00:14:37,714
Eun Ji,

394
00:14:37,715 --> 00:14:38,954
- we messed this up.
- We messed it up?

395
00:14:38,955 --> 00:14:40,054
- We messed it up. Please stop.
- We really did.

396
00:14:40,055 --> 00:14:41,125
Eun Ji, let's switch places again.

397
00:14:41,725 --> 00:14:42,755
Let's switch again.

398
00:14:43,055 --> 00:14:44,825
It's still not working. What do we do?

399
00:14:45,395 --> 00:14:46,854
(4th attempt)

400
00:14:46,855 --> 00:14:48,925
Keep the length even and take it slow.

401
00:14:49,025 --> 00:14:51,135
(6th attempt)

402
00:14:51,195 --> 00:14:52,334
Here we go.

403
00:14:52,335 --> 00:14:53,335
(7th attempt)

404
00:14:53,336 --> 00:14:54,465
Director Ye Seul, this is hard.

405
00:14:54,935 --> 00:14:57,434
- You can do it.
- Why is it so sticky?

406
00:14:57,435 --> 00:14:58,934
I think we used it too many times.

407
00:14:58,935 --> 00:15:00,375
- It developed too much gluten.
- Yes.

408
00:15:01,305 --> 00:15:03,575
(Tired)

409
00:15:03,645 --> 00:15:04,915
Young Ji, I have a good feeling about this.

410
00:15:05,545 --> 00:15:08,515
Why don't you adjust it in the water when it comes out?

411
00:15:08,915 --> 00:15:10,584
- I should.
- You can adjust it in the water.

412
00:15:10,585 --> 00:15:12,315
- Okay, let's try that.
- Yes.

413
00:15:13,015 --> 00:15:14,015
This is our last try.

414
00:15:14,425 --> 00:15:16,085
- Stretching it in the water.
- In the water.

415
00:15:16,855 --> 00:15:17,855
In the water.

416
00:15:17,856 --> 00:15:18,924
(The shaper is back on.)

417
00:15:18,925 --> 00:15:20,055
It's working.

418
00:15:20,325 --> 00:15:21,325
- Yes.
- It's working.

419
00:15:21,865 --> 00:15:23,294
- While you shape it...
- This...

420
00:15:23,295 --> 00:15:26,365
- This should be enough.
- That's good.

421
00:15:27,065 --> 00:15:28,705
That's great.

422
00:15:28,865 --> 00:15:30,105
Perfect. It really worked.

423
00:15:30,305 --> 00:15:32,134
We got it.

424
00:15:32,135 --> 00:15:34,174
I ran the rice cake through the machine without breaking it.

425
00:15:34,175 --> 00:15:35,275
Doesn't it look amazing?

426
00:15:35,645 --> 00:15:36,744
- How is it?
- Isn't it amazing?

427
00:15:36,745 --> 00:15:38,644
- Nice.
- That was nice.

428
00:15:38,645 --> 00:15:40,115
- You did such a great job.
- It looks beautiful.

429
00:15:40,215 --> 00:15:41,385
(It's time to taste the freshly made rice cake.)

430
00:15:41,745 --> 00:15:42,745
How is it?

431
00:15:42,745 --> 00:15:43,745
(Exclaiming)

432
00:15:44,615 --> 00:15:46,185
(Humming)

433
00:15:46,415 --> 00:15:48,155
- It's delicious.
- It's so good.

434
00:15:49,485 --> 00:15:53,455
(Completely absorbed in eating)

435
00:15:53,595 --> 00:15:54,764
(Exclaiming)

436
00:15:54,765 --> 00:15:56,724
- How is it?
- It's amazing.

437
00:15:56,725 --> 00:15:57,725
(I made it, but it's really good.)

438
00:15:57,726 --> 00:16:01,335
Are we running a tteokbokki place or a rice cake shop?

439
00:16:01,435 --> 00:16:02,664
- A tteokbokki place.
- Or both.

440
00:16:02,665 --> 00:16:04,334
(The question naturally comes up after 2 hours of making rice cakes.)

441
00:16:04,335 --> 00:16:05,634
Just because...

442
00:16:05,635 --> 00:16:08,304
I said I wanted to make rice cakes by hand,

443
00:16:08,305 --> 00:16:09,874
you went and got the rice cake shaper,

444
00:16:09,875 --> 00:16:11,414
the steamer, and the grinder.

445
00:16:11,415 --> 00:16:13,675
Isn't this a little too much?

446
00:16:14,115 --> 00:16:15,944
With all these machines,

447
00:16:15,945 --> 00:16:18,285
spending eight hours straight making rice cakes...

448
00:16:18,415 --> 00:16:19,714
and cutting them...

449
00:16:19,715 --> 00:16:21,424
It really shocked me...

450
00:16:21,425 --> 00:16:22,484
when Young Ji messaged me and said...

451
00:16:22,485 --> 00:16:24,154
I was just talking.

452
00:16:24,155 --> 00:16:26,354
Young Ji, when did you say you wanted to make rice cakes?

453
00:16:26,355 --> 00:16:29,064
I want to make 100,000 dollars or even 1 million dollars.

454
00:16:29,065 --> 00:16:30,894
I want to make rice cakes from scratch.

455
00:16:30,895 --> 00:16:33,434
I even want to start a fire with tinder.

456
00:16:33,435 --> 00:16:34,435
But you told me...

457
00:16:34,436 --> 00:16:35,664
Don't take everything I say literally.

458
00:16:35,665 --> 00:16:37,164
Since when did you start believing everything I say?

459
00:16:37,165 --> 00:16:38,874
Please understand her. She's being delirious...

460
00:16:38,875 --> 00:16:41,204
- from exhaustion.
- This is seriously hard work.

461
00:16:41,205 --> 00:16:42,905
Everyone says fresh rice cakes taste the best.

462
00:16:43,305 --> 00:16:45,044
Young Ji will do it, but...

463
00:16:45,045 --> 00:16:46,145
(Screaming)

464
00:16:46,975 --> 00:16:48,814
Please understand her.

465
00:16:48,815 --> 00:16:49,915
Who said I wanted to make rice cakes myself?

466
00:16:50,215 --> 00:16:52,555
Who said I wanted to do it?

467
00:16:52,785 --> 00:16:55,084
I just wanted to do the cool part at the end of slicing it.

468
00:16:55,085 --> 00:16:56,584
Who said I wanted to make baekseolgi...

469
00:16:56,585 --> 00:16:58,554
and grind the rice into flour?

470
00:16:58,555 --> 00:17:00,024
(The head chef finally unleashes her winning rant.)

471
00:17:00,025 --> 00:17:02,665
- We can do it.
- Get rid of all these machines.

472
00:17:02,925 --> 00:17:04,594
But if anyone leaves even one rice cake behind...

473
00:17:04,595 --> 00:17:06,795
Do you really think I won't chase them down?

474
00:17:07,365 --> 00:17:09,765
Don't you dare leave a single rice cake.

475
00:17:10,205 --> 00:17:11,434
Yu Jin, write down the names of everyone who leaves rice cakes.

476
00:17:11,435 --> 00:17:12,774
Put them on the blacklist.

477
00:17:12,775 --> 00:17:13,775
Okay.

478
00:17:14,135 --> 00:17:15,975
(After calming down, it's time to make jeolpyeon.)

479
00:17:16,245 --> 00:17:17,245
(While Young Ji is still ranting)

480
00:17:17,246 --> 00:17:19,514
- Nice.
- Could you stick it in once?

481
00:17:19,515 --> 00:17:20,614
- How did it turn out?
- It looks good.

482
00:17:20,615 --> 00:17:21,914
- It turned out well.
- It turned out well.

483
00:17:21,915 --> 00:17:22,985
It's perfect.

484
00:17:23,185 --> 00:17:24,185
(Switching to the jeolpyeon nozzle)

485
00:17:24,185 --> 00:17:25,185
It's done.

486
00:17:25,186 --> 00:17:26,654
- Adjust it to jeolpyeon?
- It's done.

487
00:17:26,655 --> 00:17:27,655
I can't wait to find out.

488
00:17:27,656 --> 00:17:29,554
(A cute little piece of jeolpyeon peeks out.)

489
00:17:29,555 --> 00:17:31,555
Thanks to you, it's coming out fast and smoothly.

490
00:17:31,755 --> 00:17:32,855
Eun Ji, it's perfect.

491
00:17:32,995 --> 00:17:34,664
- It looks incredible.
- Eun Ji, you're doing well.

492
00:17:34,665 --> 00:17:35,665
It's amazing.

493
00:17:35,666 --> 00:17:36,694
(Fuelled by compliments, she works even harder.)

494
00:17:36,695 --> 00:17:37,695
(It's nice and plump.)

495
00:17:37,696 --> 00:17:38,895
- Look how fat it is.
- Yes.

496
00:17:39,695 --> 00:17:40,865
This is good.

497
00:17:41,635 --> 00:17:43,464
- All the ingredients are in.
- Nice.

498
00:17:43,465 --> 00:17:44,905
Young Ji, it looks so pretty.

499
00:17:45,605 --> 00:17:47,304
(Perfectly shaped jeolpyeon)

500
00:17:47,305 --> 00:17:49,145
- It came out really nicely.
- I can't believe it.

501
00:17:49,505 --> 00:17:50,704
- Unbelievable.
- Nice.

502
00:17:50,705 --> 00:17:51,714
- We did a great job.
- I agree.

503
00:17:51,715 --> 00:17:52,815
Take photos. It looks beautiful.

504
00:17:53,315 --> 00:17:54,644
Eun Ji, you're the best.

505
00:17:54,645 --> 00:17:56,784
Let me know when you're ready to learn how to clean that.

506
00:17:56,785 --> 00:17:58,055
- What?
- How to clean it.

507
00:18:00,115 --> 00:18:02,085
(Cleaning is the foundation of cooking.)

508
00:18:02,155 --> 00:18:03,554
Peeling this off is...

509
00:18:03,555 --> 00:18:04,895
- oddly satisfying.
- I know.

510
00:18:05,725 --> 00:18:07,994
I'm sorry for saying I wanted to make rice cakes.

511
00:18:07,995 --> 00:18:09,124
I didn't mean it literally.

512
00:18:09,125 --> 00:18:10,795
I didn't expect anyone to listen to me.

513
00:18:12,095 --> 00:18:13,935
I sincerely apologise.

514
00:18:14,165 --> 00:18:15,665
We can do it. We'll help you.

515
00:18:16,135 --> 00:18:17,404
Will you help me?

516
00:18:17,405 --> 00:18:19,604
- We can do it.
- Can you really do it?

517
00:18:19,605 --> 00:18:20,775
Hey, GG!

518
00:18:21,005 --> 00:18:24,305
(Singing)

519
00:18:24,405 --> 00:18:25,774
(Shall we start?)

520
00:18:25,775 --> 00:18:27,814
(Oh, my. Look at her)

521
00:18:27,815 --> 00:18:29,545
- Head Chef, keep working.
- Okay.

522
00:18:30,085 --> 00:18:31,655
(Okay...)

523
00:18:31,715 --> 00:18:33,514
- Yu Jin.
- Yes?

524
00:18:33,515 --> 00:18:34,555
How are you doing?

525
00:18:35,025 --> 00:18:37,225
The sink is really low.

526
00:18:37,485 --> 00:18:38,824
- Okay.
- It's too low.

527
00:18:38,825 --> 00:18:40,125
Do you want a step stool?

528
00:18:40,295 --> 00:18:41,825
No, it's okay.

529
00:18:42,565 --> 00:18:44,424
Eun Ji, the weather is beautiful today.

530
00:18:44,425 --> 00:18:45,665
- Yes.
- I hope that it doesn't rain.

531
00:18:46,565 --> 00:18:48,334
(Scrubbing)

532
00:18:48,335 --> 00:18:50,335
This reminds me of my old part-time job.

533
00:18:51,005 --> 00:18:52,274
Making rice cakes takes...

534
00:18:52,275 --> 00:18:54,005
more people than I thought.

535
00:18:54,475 --> 00:18:59,145
(With this many tools to clean)

536
00:18:59,415 --> 00:19:00,914
So this is what running a business is like.

537
00:19:00,915 --> 00:19:02,845
(Cleaning up is just as much work as making the rice cakes.)

538
00:19:03,045 --> 00:19:04,444
Yu Jin, hold on.

539
00:19:04,445 --> 00:19:05,915
Do we have to clean all this every single day?

540
00:19:06,015 --> 00:19:07,684
(That's right...)

541
00:19:07,685 --> 00:19:10,255
It's because we aren't the head chef.

542
00:19:10,885 --> 00:19:13,195
- That's why...
- But...

543
00:19:14,125 --> 00:19:15,595
we're the ones doing it.

544
00:19:15,995 --> 00:19:17,465
Making rice cakes is no joke.

545
00:19:17,595 --> 00:19:19,465
- Maybe that's why they're so good.
- Right.

546
00:19:19,795 --> 00:19:21,065
Korean rice cakes deserve...

547
00:19:21,135 --> 00:19:23,035
way more recognition.

548
00:19:23,805 --> 00:19:26,034
Cooking shows are exhausting on a whole different level.

549
00:19:26,035 --> 00:19:27,334
- We haven't even started cooking.
- Right.

550
00:19:27,335 --> 00:19:28,345
Exactly.

551
00:19:28,975 --> 00:19:33,044
Thinking about doing this every single day...

552
00:19:33,045 --> 00:19:34,714
Huge respect to everyone who runs their own business.

553
00:19:34,715 --> 00:19:36,744
Maybe it's hard because it's our first day.

554
00:19:36,745 --> 00:19:38,655
If we get used to it tomorrow...

555
00:19:39,385 --> 00:19:40,385
Never mind.

556
00:19:41,985 --> 00:19:43,685
Our business is over for today.

557
00:19:43,985 --> 00:19:46,355
We haven't even cooked anything yet. I'm terrified.

558
00:19:47,095 --> 00:19:49,094
- Let's eat together.
- Let's gather.

559
00:19:49,095 --> 00:19:50,925
- Gather up, everyone.
- Gosh.

560
00:19:51,795 --> 00:19:53,565
- Enjoy your food.
- Enjoy your food.

561
00:19:53,765 --> 00:19:55,565
- Thank you for the food.
- It's delicious.

562
00:19:56,505 --> 00:19:57,705
The view is incredible.

563
00:19:59,735 --> 00:20:03,105
(They have been stuck in the kitchen all day, but...)

564
00:20:05,345 --> 00:20:08,314
(Space Rice Cake sits in front of a breathtaking ocean view.)

565
00:20:08,315 --> 00:20:10,784
This dried laver is excellent.

566
00:20:10,785 --> 00:20:12,184
- I like the dried laver too.
- Yes.

567
00:20:12,185 --> 00:20:13,255
It's delicious.

568
00:20:14,085 --> 00:20:15,585
I guess there's always room for food.

569
00:20:16,125 --> 00:20:17,454
- We must eat to survive.
- We worked hard, after all.

570
00:20:17,455 --> 00:20:18,455
Right.

571
00:20:18,895 --> 00:20:20,454
All we did was run the rice cake dough through the machine.

572
00:20:20,455 --> 00:20:22,125
(Already wiped out after running the dough through the machine)

573
00:20:22,825 --> 00:20:25,095
It's the quietest variety show we've ever done.

574
00:20:25,535 --> 00:20:27,465
It's practically white noise at this point.

575
00:20:29,935 --> 00:20:31,834
On "Earth Arcade," the harder it was,

576
00:20:31,835 --> 00:20:32,875
the bigger the success was.

577
00:20:33,375 --> 00:20:34,745
How successful will this be?

578
00:20:35,745 --> 00:20:38,144
- How much harder...
- What if no one watches it?

579
00:20:38,145 --> 00:20:39,244
(We want to succeed.)

580
00:20:39,245 --> 00:20:40,275
That's so funny.

581
00:20:40,575 --> 00:20:41,615
I'm full.

582
00:20:42,885 --> 00:20:44,115
Are you full?

583
00:20:44,345 --> 00:20:45,385
- Yes.
- Me too.

584
00:20:45,455 --> 00:20:46,585
Really?

585
00:20:48,555 --> 00:20:50,925
(Current Time: 3pm)

586
00:20:51,255 --> 00:20:53,724
We'll be doing a soft opening.

587
00:20:53,725 --> 00:20:55,294
- Oh, no.
- A soft opening.

588
00:20:55,295 --> 00:20:57,894
- Is it like a practice service?
- Yes.

589
00:20:57,895 --> 00:20:59,465
(A final check before the opening)

590
00:20:59,695 --> 00:21:01,334
- First, we need a name.
- Yes.

591
00:21:01,335 --> 00:21:02,765
We need to name our place.

592
00:21:03,305 --> 00:21:05,034
For now, let's just call it "Lee Young Ji Tteokbokki."

593
00:21:05,035 --> 00:21:06,935
- For now.
- "Lee Young Ji Tteokbokki."

594
00:21:07,135 --> 00:21:09,144
This is its pseudonym,

595
00:21:09,145 --> 00:21:10,345
"Ghost Pepper Tteokbokki."

596
00:21:10,475 --> 00:21:13,415
Originally, I wanted to call it, "Don't Eat Ghost Pepper Tteokbokki."

597
00:21:13,545 --> 00:21:16,484
"Don't eat ghost pepper tteokbokki, it's a challenge."

598
00:21:16,485 --> 00:21:17,715
Can you all do that?

599
00:21:18,615 --> 00:21:20,754
- Come on, Eun Ji.
- You need a working title.

600
00:21:20,755 --> 00:21:22,384
"Challenge: Beat Lee Young Ji."

601
00:21:22,385 --> 00:21:24,825
- Right.
- "Challenge: Beat Lee Young Ji."

602
00:21:25,025 --> 00:21:28,594
"Don't eat ghost pepper tteokbokki, it's a challenge."

603
00:21:28,595 --> 00:21:29,695
Well done.

604
00:21:30,425 --> 00:21:32,594
- And pollack roe and clam pasta.
- Pollack roe...

605
00:21:32,595 --> 00:21:34,735
- Pollack roe and clam pasta.
- Pollack roe and clam pasta.

606
00:21:35,305 --> 00:21:39,034
It's tiramisu, but it has chestnuts and rice cake.

607
00:21:39,035 --> 00:21:40,905
How about "Chestnut Tyranno?"

608
00:21:42,845 --> 00:21:44,674
Chestnut Tyranno!

609
00:21:44,675 --> 00:21:45,675
(The comedian version of "Chestnut Tyranno")

610
00:21:45,945 --> 00:21:47,414
(A dinosaur from the Cretaceous appears in Goheung.)

611
00:21:47,415 --> 00:21:49,385
Like the dinosaur.

612
00:21:50,415 --> 00:21:51,654
(Confidence is half the recipe when naming dishes.)

613
00:21:51,655 --> 00:21:53,255
Like a Tyrannosaurus.

614
00:21:53,855 --> 00:21:56,225
- I like this idea.
- Isn't it nice?

615
00:21:56,825 --> 00:21:58,024
We'll name it Chestnut Tyranno.

616
00:21:58,025 --> 00:21:59,194
Don't be ridiculous.

617
00:21:59,195 --> 00:22:00,595
It's just a working title.

618
00:22:00,925 --> 00:22:01,964
A working title.

619
00:22:01,965 --> 00:22:03,665
Yes, as a working title.

620
00:22:04,125 --> 00:22:06,035
You can say it like this. "Chestnut Tyranno."

621
00:22:06,235 --> 00:22:07,235
- "Chestnut Tyranno."
- How about...

622
00:22:07,236 --> 00:22:08,864
(Chestnutericano)

623
00:22:08,865 --> 00:22:10,464
(Lee Young Ji Tteokbokki, pollack roe and clam pasta...)

624
00:22:10,465 --> 00:22:12,335
(The soft opening menu is complete.)

625
00:22:13,205 --> 00:22:14,774
- Here we go.
- Okay.

626
00:22:14,775 --> 00:22:15,775
(The preparation starts.)

627
00:22:15,776 --> 00:22:17,005
This is...

628
00:22:17,175 --> 00:22:19,014
the perfect amount of consistency.

629
00:22:19,015 --> 00:22:20,045
(The head chef is making her signature sauce.)

630
00:22:20,175 --> 00:22:21,275
Is this enough for today?

631
00:22:21,615 --> 00:22:22,815
Yes, that's perfect.

632
00:22:22,985 --> 00:22:24,184
I chopped them well, right?

633
00:22:24,185 --> 00:22:25,285
Mimi is the best.

634
00:22:25,715 --> 00:22:27,984
(The sous-chef preps the ingredients with love.)

635
00:22:27,985 --> 00:22:30,425
(Encouraged by the compliment, she chops away even harder.)

636
00:22:30,625 --> 00:22:31,725
I'll check on the rice cakes.

637
00:22:32,025 --> 00:22:33,925
I look like So Ji Sub today, and I like it.

638
00:22:36,025 --> 00:22:38,994
(Ji Sub falls silent.)

639
00:22:38,995 --> 00:22:40,565
Eun Ji, the rice cakes...

640
00:22:40,865 --> 00:22:41,935
What's wrong?

641
00:22:42,165 --> 00:22:44,065
- My goodness.
- What's the matter?

642
00:22:44,635 --> 00:22:46,175
They're stuck to the plastic.

643
00:22:47,235 --> 00:22:48,374
Goodness.

644
00:22:48,375 --> 00:22:50,804
No, take them off slowly.

645
00:22:50,805 --> 00:22:51,814
(Now we have another problem sticking to us.)

646
00:22:51,815 --> 00:22:55,385
(The rice cakes still refuse to cooperate.)

647
00:22:55,485 --> 00:22:57,744
I'm worried about the baekseolgi.

648
00:22:57,745 --> 00:22:58,754
(The baekseolgi...)

649
00:22:58,755 --> 00:23:00,655
This can't be helped.

650
00:23:01,255 --> 00:23:02,454
(Sighing)

651
00:23:02,455 --> 00:23:04,055
- Are you okay?
- What kind of sound was that?

652
00:23:04,685 --> 00:23:06,694
- Everything depends on running...
- The rice cake...

653
00:23:06,695 --> 00:23:08,664
the rice cake through the machine properly.

654
00:23:08,665 --> 00:23:09,964
Who would've thought...

655
00:23:09,965 --> 00:23:11,394
we'd be making rice cakes ourselves?

656
00:23:11,395 --> 00:23:12,395
(No one saw it coming.)

657
00:23:12,396 --> 00:23:14,934
Who suggested making rice cakes from scratch anyway?

658
00:23:14,935 --> 00:23:16,364
(Crying)

659
00:23:16,365 --> 00:23:19,635
Since when did you start taking everything I say so seriously?

660
00:23:19,975 --> 00:23:21,275
It's because you're the head chef.

661
00:23:21,535 --> 00:23:25,244
(Reconsidering what it really means to be the head chef)

662
00:23:25,245 --> 00:23:26,315
Chef.

663
00:23:27,475 --> 00:23:29,645
- You became awfully quiet.
- What?

664
00:23:30,015 --> 00:23:32,354
These rice cakes are being so annoying.

665
00:23:32,355 --> 00:23:33,814
(It's because the rice cakes are annoying.)

666
00:23:33,815 --> 00:23:36,385
I told you. We should've just bought them.

667
00:23:37,425 --> 00:23:38,824
(Sighing)

668
00:23:38,825 --> 00:23:40,525
(Laughing)

669
00:23:40,625 --> 00:23:43,395
I'm sorry. It's my bad.

670
00:23:44,295 --> 00:23:45,995
Why isn't it coming out?

671
00:23:47,435 --> 00:23:50,605
(The staff's frustration keeps piling up.)

672
00:23:51,205 --> 00:23:52,205
This brat...

673
00:23:52,206 --> 00:23:53,304
(She's not cursing.)

674
00:23:53,305 --> 00:23:55,444
Can someone post a job listing for a part-timer?

675
00:23:55,445 --> 00:23:57,744
Maybe on some secondhand marketplace.

676
00:23:57,745 --> 00:23:59,214
Director, instead of giving us feedback,

677
00:23:59,215 --> 00:24:00,645
get in here.

678
00:24:01,515 --> 00:24:03,415
(Even the youngest tries to keep smiling.)

679
00:24:03,545 --> 00:24:04,845
My goodness.

680
00:24:04,985 --> 00:24:06,584
(Even the skies are against them.)

681
00:24:06,585 --> 00:24:07,614
Are you okay?

682
00:24:07,615 --> 00:24:08,924
Mimi, do you need help?

683
00:24:08,925 --> 00:24:10,125
(Even the trusted sous-chef)

684
00:24:10,855 --> 00:24:11,995
It's not open.

685
00:24:12,725 --> 00:24:14,895
Wait a minute.

686
00:24:15,625 --> 00:24:17,564
What if people watching this show think...

687
00:24:17,565 --> 00:24:19,165
that we're idiots?

688
00:24:22,335 --> 00:24:23,805
- My gosh, look at this.
- Here we go.

689
00:24:23,865 --> 00:24:25,604
- One, two, three.
- One, two, three.

690
00:24:25,605 --> 00:24:27,135
(The preparation is complete.)

691
00:24:27,505 --> 00:24:28,674
(Exhausted)

692
00:24:28,675 --> 00:24:29,905
I'm only checking my phone now.

693
00:24:30,575 --> 00:24:32,775
I looked at it at noon. I look at it after five hours.

694
00:24:33,615 --> 00:24:36,014
- What time is it?
- It's 5:52pm.

695
00:24:36,015 --> 00:24:37,345
- Don't talk to me anymore.
- Okay.

696
00:24:37,985 --> 00:24:39,554
Hey, ladies.

697
00:24:39,555 --> 00:24:41,055
- Yes?
- Can we do this once?

698
00:24:41,315 --> 00:24:42,754
- It's 5:52pm.
- Where we seat our customers...

699
00:24:42,755 --> 00:24:44,425
Ladies, what are you doing?

700
00:24:45,195 --> 00:24:46,224
What's the problem?

701
00:24:46,225 --> 00:24:47,954
Ladies, could you get up for a minute?

702
00:24:47,955 --> 00:24:49,264
We still have eight minutes.

703
00:24:49,265 --> 00:24:50,794
Let's just check where we'll seat our customers.

704
00:24:50,795 --> 00:24:52,234
- That's the only...
- You're such an MZ kid.

705
00:24:52,235 --> 00:24:54,364
Shouldn't we figure out where to seat our customers?

706
00:24:54,365 --> 00:24:56,134
- Okay, I'll read the vibe.
- The vibe?

707
00:24:56,135 --> 00:24:57,165
Okay.

708
00:24:57,235 --> 00:24:59,235
Don't read the vibe and get moving

709
00:24:59,505 --> 00:25:00,874
- She's really bossy.
- Is there no medium size?

710
00:25:00,875 --> 00:25:02,305
She told me not to sell the medium size.

711
00:25:02,545 --> 00:25:03,545
Boss.

712
00:25:03,546 --> 00:25:04,944
- Boss.
- Yes?

713
00:25:04,945 --> 00:25:06,274
If you keep treating me like this, I'll quit.

714
00:25:06,275 --> 00:25:07,974
- Boss, who else would work here...
- You know what?

715
00:25:07,975 --> 00:25:09,414
- besides us?
- She's right.

716
00:25:09,415 --> 00:25:10,415
Go ahead and quit.

717
00:25:10,416 --> 00:25:11,584
Report me to the labour office.

718
00:25:11,585 --> 00:25:13,684
- Listen, boss.
- I'll post you on Instagram.

719
00:25:13,685 --> 00:25:14,685
"Darn it."

720
00:25:14,855 --> 00:25:17,355
"That MZ part-timer totally ruined my day."

721
00:25:17,525 --> 00:25:19,254
- I can post too.
- Go ahead.

722
00:25:19,255 --> 00:25:20,324
- Me too.
- "Darn it."

723
00:25:20,325 --> 00:25:21,864
"My boss has lost it."

724
00:25:21,865 --> 00:25:23,765
"Darn it, my part-timer has lost it."

725
00:25:23,965 --> 00:25:25,634
- We can do it too.
- Okay, bring it on.

726
00:25:25,635 --> 00:25:26,735
- These days...
- Goodness.

727
00:25:27,095 --> 00:25:28,704
- It's not easy.
- Let's see who backs down first.

728
00:25:28,705 --> 00:25:29,904
Just scrap the whole thing.

729
00:25:29,905 --> 00:25:31,165
(The soft opening begins.)

730
00:25:31,265 --> 00:25:34,205
(On today's menu)

731
00:25:35,305 --> 00:25:38,145
(Lee Young Ji Tteokbokki)

732
00:25:38,945 --> 00:25:41,985
(Simmered for 10 minutes in our handmade sauce)

733
00:25:42,885 --> 00:25:45,015
(Thick garaetteok)

734
00:25:46,715 --> 00:25:49,125
(Topped with an assortment of fried seafood)

735
00:25:50,385 --> 00:25:52,825
(Next is Young Ji's dish made with pride and joy)

736
00:25:54,325 --> 00:25:55,494
(Don't Eat Ghost Pepper Tteokbokki, It's a Challenge)

737
00:25:55,495 --> 00:25:56,495
(Beat Lee Young Ji)

738
00:25:56,995 --> 00:26:00,665
(The challenge menu that brings extreme spiciness)

739
00:26:01,135 --> 00:26:04,305
(Next is Sous-chef Mimi's signature dish.)

740
00:26:05,075 --> 00:26:07,135
(Pollack roe and clam pasta)

741
00:26:08,275 --> 00:26:10,574
(Refreshing clam...)

742
00:26:10,575 --> 00:26:13,375
(and thinly sliced jeolpyeon)

743
00:26:14,115 --> 00:26:17,345
(Creating a fantastic taste with pollack roe)

744
00:26:17,745 --> 00:26:20,255
(As for dessert, it's Chestnut Tyranno.)

745
00:26:21,385 --> 00:26:23,355
(Sweet chestnut cream...)

746
00:26:24,085 --> 00:26:26,425
(topped with a snowfall of roasted chestnut powder)

747
00:26:26,955 --> 00:26:29,095
(Finished with a whole chestnut)

748
00:26:29,325 --> 00:26:30,864
