994
00:34:10,985 --> 00:34:11,985
- "Crunchy?"
- How about "zesty?"

995
00:34:11,986 --> 00:34:13,955
- "Zesty" sounds good.
- Zesty.

996
00:34:14,125 --> 00:34:16,424
(Fancy coffee slushy)

997
00:34:16,425 --> 00:34:18,664
(Zesty pomegranate slushy)

998
00:34:18,665 --> 00:34:21,135
(The menu is complete.)

999
00:34:21,295 --> 00:34:22,965
Hello. Honesty.

1000
00:34:23,105 --> 00:34:24,204
- Humility.
- Humility.

1001
00:34:24,205 --> 00:34:26,075
- Ahk.
- Ahk.

1002
00:34:26,275 --> 00:34:28,975
(Their business hasn't even opened yet,)

1003
00:34:29,205 --> 00:34:31,605
(but today was a very long day.)

1004
00:34:31,745 --> 00:34:32,745
That must be it.

1005
00:34:32,746 --> 00:34:34,175
- It's our lodging.
- We're here.

1006
00:34:35,015 --> 00:34:36,015
The problem is...

1007
00:34:36,016 --> 00:34:38,215
how we'll run the rice cake dough through the machine tomorrow.

1008
00:34:38,645 --> 00:34:41,114
How will we make the rice cakes tomorrow?

1009
00:34:41,115 --> 00:34:43,054
That machine is unbelievably delicate.

1010
00:34:43,055 --> 00:34:44,725
- Seriously.
- Yes.

1011
00:34:45,795 --> 00:34:48,454
I'm so scared for tomorrow. I'm an anxious type of head chef.

1012
00:34:48,455 --> 00:34:50,565
(She's worrying about herself.)

1013
00:34:50,695 --> 00:34:53,495
I'm about to lose it. Actually, I'm terrified.

1014
00:34:55,035 --> 00:34:57,905
(The night filled with anxiety comes to an end.)

1015
00:34:58,935 --> 00:35:01,605
(The morning of opening day finally arrived.)

1016
00:35:02,975 --> 00:35:05,205
(As if celebrating the grand opening,)

1017
00:35:06,475 --> 00:35:10,685
(today's weather is gloomy.)

1018
00:35:11,545 --> 00:35:13,854
(On a day like this,)

1019
00:35:13,855 --> 00:35:15,955
(will anyone come?)

1020
00:35:16,855 --> 00:35:19,725
(Early morning at the accommodation)

1021
00:35:20,655 --> 00:35:22,094
- Hello.
- Young Ji.

1022
00:35:22,095 --> 00:35:24,124
- You put on your makeup.
- I did.

1023
00:35:24,125 --> 00:35:25,295
Gosh, it's raining.

1024
00:35:25,465 --> 00:35:27,565
- Hello.
- I'm coming down with something.

1025
00:35:28,365 --> 00:35:30,165
(The truth is, last night...)

1026
00:35:30,535 --> 00:35:32,904
Running a business requires so much preparation.

1027
00:35:32,905 --> 00:35:34,174
Can anyone keep up...

1028
00:35:34,175 --> 00:35:35,434
- with this schedule?
- How many times did we do this?

1029
00:35:35,435 --> 00:35:37,545
This chestnut cream is killing me.

1030
00:35:37,875 --> 00:35:40,374
Why does the day feel so long?

1031
00:35:40,375 --> 00:35:43,285
(The Earth Arcaders were occupied throughout the day.)

1032
00:35:43,515 --> 00:35:45,084
- Did you get some sleep?
- What?

1033
00:35:45,085 --> 00:35:47,614
I woke up once at 3am, 4am, 5am, and 6am.

1034
00:35:47,615 --> 00:35:48,884
You woke up every single hour?

1035
00:35:48,885 --> 00:35:51,254
When I woke up at 3am, I thought that it was 6am.

1036
00:35:51,255 --> 00:35:53,395
- Did you sleep well?
- Did you sleep well?

1037
00:35:53,595 --> 00:35:56,495
- You look beautiful today.
- Do I look cute?

1038
00:35:57,265 --> 00:35:58,664
If I sprint from here to there at full speed,

1039
00:35:58,665 --> 00:36:00,034
would it take about a minute and a half?

1040
00:36:00,035 --> 00:36:01,834
- Try it.
- Try it, Young Ji.

1041
00:36:01,835 --> 00:36:02,965
No, don't.

1042
00:36:03,565 --> 00:36:06,035
Young Ji, don't waste your energy. We have a lot to do.

1043
00:36:06,135 --> 00:36:07,574
- Young Ji...
- You guys are terrible.

1044
00:36:07,575 --> 00:36:09,245
Please calm down.

1045
00:36:10,305 --> 00:36:11,474
- We're almost there.
- Gosh.

1046
00:36:11,475 --> 00:36:13,174
- What's the matter?
- It really hurts.

1047
00:36:13,175 --> 00:36:16,214
Are you pretending to be hurt to avoid going to work?

1048
00:36:16,215 --> 00:36:17,985
(Groaning)

1049
00:36:18,685 --> 00:36:21,185
- I don't think I can go to work.
- Stop it.

1050
00:36:22,215 --> 00:36:23,655
We're at work. I feel so good.

1051
00:36:25,895 --> 00:36:27,255
Young Ji, go in already.

1052
00:36:28,155 --> 00:36:29,264
I don't want to work.

1053
00:36:29,265 --> 00:36:31,565
(Arriving at work feeling lighthearted)

1054
00:36:32,095 --> 00:36:33,165
When it's raining

1055
00:36:33,335 --> 00:36:34,394
(Now it's time to prep.)

1056
00:36:34,395 --> 00:36:35,905
And the music is playing

1057
00:36:36,835 --> 00:36:38,935
Everyone, put on your aprons and get to your stations.

1058
00:36:39,405 --> 00:36:40,935
- I forgot my apron.
- What?

1059
00:36:41,275 --> 00:36:43,045
- I forgot my apron. I'll run home.
- Me too.

1060
00:36:46,915 --> 00:36:49,145
(So it began 30 seconds after arriving at work.)

1061
00:36:50,015 --> 00:36:53,115
(A self-chase mission to find the apron)

1062
00:36:53,715 --> 00:36:57,755
(A joke came back to haunt her.)

1063
00:36:58,585 --> 00:36:59,625
Why didn't you...

1064
00:37:00,195 --> 00:37:01,655
bring your apron?

1065
00:37:01,925 --> 00:37:02,965
(Panting)

1066
00:37:03,065 --> 00:37:04,494
I don't want to run this business anymore.

1067
00:37:04,495 --> 00:37:05,495
(Her true feelings)

1068
00:37:05,496 --> 00:37:08,565
(Sprinting of anger)

1069
00:37:12,205 --> 00:37:14,604
(The aprons are safely rescued.)

1070
00:37:14,605 --> 00:37:16,175
I'm unbelievably happy.

1071
00:37:17,075 --> 00:37:18,145
I'm so happy...

1072
00:37:18,905 --> 00:37:20,245
that I could go for a bottle of soju.

1073
00:37:20,775 --> 00:37:23,085
It's raining. Wait a minute.

1074
00:37:23,645 --> 00:37:25,715
What are we going to do if it rains today?

1075
00:37:26,615 --> 00:37:28,655
Let me think before I start running again.

1076
00:37:29,455 --> 00:37:32,085
I need to hurry and prep the ingredients.

1077
00:37:33,125 --> 00:37:34,995
The rice cakes go into the steamer.

1078
00:37:35,695 --> 00:37:38,395
How do you turn on that machine again?

1079
00:37:38,725 --> 00:37:40,195
(It's called the rice cake shaper.)

1080
00:37:40,535 --> 00:37:41,735
I can't even run that fast.

1081
00:37:43,005 --> 00:37:45,365
Director, please don't abandon me.

1082
00:37:46,175 --> 00:37:47,205
Director!

1083
00:37:47,635 --> 00:37:48,774
Where are you going?

1084
00:37:48,775 --> 00:37:49,775
(Everyone fends for themselves.)

1085
00:37:52,375 --> 00:37:55,445
(Thankfully, they arrived together.)

1086
00:37:55,575 --> 00:37:57,515
(It's time to run the dough through the machine.)

1087
00:37:57,845 --> 00:37:58,845
Hey, rice cake shaper!

1088
00:38:00,455 --> 00:38:02,185
Hey you, rice cake shaper.

1089
00:38:02,655 --> 00:38:03,955
What are you doing here?

1090
00:38:06,125 --> 00:38:07,154
Are you good at pounding?

1091
00:38:07,155 --> 00:38:08,195
(Intrigued)

1092
00:38:08,295 --> 00:38:11,095
Are you good at pounding rice cakes?

1093
00:38:11,625 --> 00:38:12,795
Hey, rice cake shaper.

1094
00:38:13,135 --> 00:38:16,834
We need to get the first step right. It's making the rice cakes.

1095
00:38:16,835 --> 00:38:17,835
Right.

1096
00:38:17,836 --> 00:38:19,205
If the rice cake is off,

1097
00:38:19,575 --> 00:38:21,774
- everything else is off too.
- Even when we make tiramisu.

1098
00:38:21,775 --> 00:38:23,774
Nothing ever turns out perfectly.

1099
00:38:23,775 --> 00:38:25,045
- The rice cakes are very important.
- Right.

1100
00:38:25,705 --> 00:38:26,714
Thank you.

1101
00:38:26,715 --> 00:38:28,575
(First, they wash their hands thoroughly.)

1102
00:38:29,245 --> 00:38:31,744
- Flour team, prepare the flour.
- Yes, chef.

1103
00:38:31,745 --> 00:38:33,954
Don't we have to rinse it?

1104
00:38:33,955 --> 00:38:35,585
We need to drain out the water.

1105
00:38:36,425 --> 00:38:38,284
It got heavier after sitting overnight.

1106
00:38:38,285 --> 00:38:39,855
Relax your arms. Don't strain yourself.

1107
00:38:39,955 --> 00:38:41,594
Don't we just have to carry it?

1108
00:38:41,595 --> 00:38:42,795
You're right. One, two, three.

1109
00:38:43,895 --> 00:38:45,465
(Splash)

1110
00:38:45,865 --> 00:38:46,964
I feel a little foolish.

1111
00:38:46,965 --> 00:38:48,195
(A task that didn't need to happen in the yard)

1112
00:38:48,565 --> 00:38:49,605
Let's go.

1113
00:38:49,865 --> 00:38:52,335
- Do we leave this here?
- I'll take it later.

1114
00:38:54,005 --> 00:38:55,274
(Chuckling)

1115
00:38:55,275 --> 00:38:57,904
We look a little ridiculous right now.

1116
00:38:57,905 --> 00:38:58,974
It'll get edited out anyway.

1117
00:38:58,975 --> 00:39:00,175
(The service team's challenging future is ahead.)

1118
00:39:01,045 --> 00:39:02,915
Pour it all. One, two, three.

1119
00:39:03,545 --> 00:39:05,714
(All into the rice grinder)

1120
00:39:05,715 --> 00:39:06,854
Eun Ji, there's a lot.

1121
00:39:06,855 --> 00:39:08,555
(All into the rice grinder)

1122
00:39:09,225 --> 00:39:10,255
Here we go.

1123
00:39:10,855 --> 00:39:11,855
(The power is on.)

1124
00:39:11,856 --> 00:39:12,925
- Let's go, Eun Ji.
- You can do it.

1125
00:39:14,095 --> 00:39:16,294
- Honesty.
- Humility.

1126
00:39:16,295 --> 00:39:18,665
- Ahk.
- Ahk.

1127
00:39:19,565 --> 00:39:20,635
Who are we?

1128
00:39:21,195 --> 00:39:22,535
- Earth Arcaders.
- Earth Arcaders.

1129
00:39:23,935 --> 00:39:25,535
- We can do everything.
- We can do it.

1130
00:39:26,205 --> 00:39:27,275
There's nothing we can't do.

1131
00:39:28,135 --> 00:39:30,044
(Mixing after adding water and salt)

1132
00:39:30,045 --> 00:39:32,045
- It shouldn't clump up, right?
- Right.

1133
00:39:32,405 --> 00:39:34,114
Won't it be strained anyway?

1134
00:39:34,115 --> 00:39:37,845
Yesterday, it was okay as long as it clumped a little.

1135
00:39:38,415 --> 00:39:41,115
When the rice grinder is done, shouldn't it make a noise?

1136
00:39:42,485 --> 00:39:44,955
(Once the service team grinds the rice)

1137
00:39:45,355 --> 00:39:47,255
- Please spread it out flat.
- Okay.

1138
00:39:48,125 --> 00:39:49,724
Next is the rice cake shaper.

1139
00:39:49,725 --> 00:39:50,895
Turn on the rice cake shaper.

1140
00:39:51,595 --> 00:39:53,634
- Be careful.
- Be careful.

1141
00:39:53,635 --> 00:39:55,235
- Safety first.
- Watch out behind you.

1142
00:39:55,665 --> 00:39:57,104
Your body is your most valuable asset.

1143
00:39:57,105 --> 00:39:59,635
(The steamer starts.)

1144
00:40:00,275 --> 00:40:01,774
(A refreshing blast of steam pours out.)

1145
00:40:01,775 --> 00:40:03,304
- Chef, do we need more?
- What?

1146
00:40:03,305 --> 00:40:04,375
Should we make more?

1147
00:40:04,805 --> 00:40:06,245
Please take a look at the amount.

1148
00:40:06,845 --> 00:40:09,715
(While Mimi spreads out the rice flour)

1149
00:40:11,045 --> 00:40:12,754
Three of these for baekseolgi.

1150
00:40:12,755 --> 00:40:13,885
(While Yu Jin weighs the salt)

1151
00:40:14,615 --> 00:40:18,385
(While the head chef washes the cloth)

1152
00:40:18,725 --> 00:40:20,494
Shouldn't we put in more? It should be 1cm...

1153
00:40:20,495 --> 00:40:23,294
- Young Ji, can I use this?
- Chef, do we need to put in more?

1154
00:40:23,295 --> 00:40:25,025
- Young Ji, this...
- Wait, what?

1155
00:40:26,295 --> 00:40:29,164
Young Ji, you forgot to do one thing. Think carefully.

1156
00:40:29,165 --> 00:40:30,805
- What?
- You forgot to do one thing.

1157
00:40:31,365 --> 00:40:34,775
(Find what's wrong with this picture)

1158
00:40:40,175 --> 00:40:41,175
What?

1159
00:40:41,176 --> 00:40:42,344
(Completely innocent)

1160
00:40:42,345 --> 00:40:44,584
The whole room is getting foggy right now.

1161
00:40:44,585 --> 00:40:46,515
You didn't turn on the exhaust hood.

1162
00:40:47,155 --> 00:40:49,425
- Oh, right.
- Turn on the ventilation fan.

1163
00:40:49,585 --> 00:40:51,425
- That's good.
- I'm sorry, everyone.

1164
00:40:51,785 --> 00:40:52,794
It's okay.

1165
00:40:52,795 --> 00:40:55,395
I thought I saw a mountain spirit.

1166
00:40:55,795 --> 00:40:56,995
It's a humidifier.

1167
00:40:57,795 --> 00:40:58,995
It's nice and moist in here.

1168
00:40:59,665 --> 00:41:00,765
(Giggling)

1169
00:41:00,865 --> 00:41:03,005
It's okay. We didn't start a fire.

1170
00:41:03,765 --> 00:41:06,335
- Do we need three of these?
- This is big.

1171
00:41:06,935 --> 00:41:07,935
What?

1172
00:41:07,936 --> 00:41:09,644
(Acting strange to hide the embarrassment)

1173
00:41:09,645 --> 00:41:11,345
What? Didn't someone talk to me?

1174
00:41:12,005 --> 00:41:13,674
(Finally placing the steaming tray on the steamer)

1175
00:41:13,675 --> 00:41:14,875
- Once the steam builds up...
- I see.

1176
00:41:15,275 --> 00:41:17,214
- My gosh.
- Okay, that was nice.

1177
00:41:17,215 --> 00:41:19,354
- I got it now.
- That's good.

1178
00:41:19,355 --> 00:41:20,384
(20 minutes later)

1179
00:41:20,385 --> 00:41:21,455
Do it slowly.

1180
00:41:22,825 --> 00:41:23,854
(Gosh, it's hot.)

1181
00:41:23,855 --> 00:41:25,024
It's hot.

1182
00:41:25,025 --> 00:41:26,454
(Gosh, it's hot.)

1183
00:41:26,455 --> 00:41:27,495
Be careful.

1184
00:41:27,895 --> 00:41:30,294
- Oh, my.
- This is done.

1185
00:41:30,295 --> 00:41:31,425
(Checking the baekseolgi)

1186
00:41:31,925 --> 00:41:34,764
If it's too thin, we'll build three layers.

1187
00:41:34,765 --> 00:41:36,804
- Okay, for now...
- Let's keep going.

1188
00:41:36,805 --> 00:41:37,904
We already made it.

1189
00:41:37,905 --> 00:41:39,034
(Checking with the main team)

1190
00:41:39,035 --> 00:41:40,504
You just made a big hole in it.

1191
00:41:40,505 --> 00:41:41,705
Let it cool for now.

1192
00:41:42,235 --> 00:41:43,945
If you keep poking at it, it'll eventually come out.

1193
00:41:45,375 --> 00:41:46,774
She said, "If you keep poking at it, it'll eventually come out."

1194
00:41:46,775 --> 00:41:48,475
(She's right.)

1195
00:41:48,615 --> 00:41:51,214
When you go get groceries, please buy some eggs.

1196
00:41:51,215 --> 00:41:52,414
And some rice.

1197
00:41:52,415 --> 00:41:55,285
- You mean, microwavable rice?
- Yes. Thank you.

1198
00:41:56,225 --> 00:41:58,754
- We're going to the market.
- See you later.

1199
00:41:58,755 --> 00:41:59,955
- Be careful.
- Drive safely.

1200
00:42:00,555 --> 00:42:01,555
Be careful.

1201
00:42:02,965 --> 00:42:03,995
Stay strong.

1202
00:42:04,195 --> 00:42:05,695
What should we do now, Mimi?

1203
00:42:05,995 --> 00:42:07,864
- Let's drink some water.
- We should keep it clean.

1204
00:42:07,865 --> 00:42:09,904
Now the real battle begins.

1205
00:42:09,905 --> 00:42:12,735
We have to finish making rice cakes before they come back at 10am.

1206
00:42:13,475 --> 00:42:15,774
(Meanwhile, the shopping team heads to the supermarket.)

1207
00:42:15,775 --> 00:42:18,005
Gosh, it's pouring.

1208
00:42:19,375 --> 00:42:21,575
I'm glad that there aren't many cars at this time.

1209
00:42:21,945 --> 00:42:23,015
I know.

1210
00:42:24,815 --> 00:42:26,555
There's H Mart. Is that a farmers' market?

1211
00:42:27,815 --> 00:42:31,224
This is the downtown area. There's a karaoke bar called Venus.

1212
00:42:31,225 --> 00:42:32,825
Eun Ji, there's a cafe.

1213
00:42:33,395 --> 00:42:34,395
(They're beyond excited for their first outing.)

1214
00:42:34,396 --> 00:42:35,824
There's a convenience store.

1215
00:42:35,825 --> 00:42:38,165
(They're beyond excited for their first outing.)

1216
00:42:38,595 --> 00:42:39,834
The supermarket is big.

1217
00:42:39,835 --> 00:42:40,835
(They arrive at the supermarket.)

1218
00:42:41,565 --> 00:42:44,465
- Yu Jin, what should we buy first?
- Over here...

1219
00:42:44,965 --> 00:42:46,704
I don't think we need vegetables.

1220
00:42:46,705 --> 00:42:48,374
- Vegetables? Eggs.
- Eggs.

1221
00:42:48,375 --> 00:42:50,405
Let's head over to the fresh food and dairy section.

1222
00:42:51,045 --> 00:42:53,244
We might as well buy an entire tray, right?

1223
00:42:53,245 --> 00:42:55,575
- It will take one month anyway.
- Right. They don't go bad easily.

1224
00:42:56,315 --> 00:42:58,385
Yu Jin, I'll bring the microwavable rice. Stay here.

1225
00:42:59,785 --> 00:43:01,455
(They also buy microwavable rice.)

1226
00:43:01,585 --> 00:43:03,455
(Grocery list: Eggs, microwavable rice)

1227
00:43:04,055 --> 00:43:06,294
There should be beef loin in the frozen food section.

1228
00:43:06,295 --> 00:43:07,625
- You're right.
- Shall we get it there?

1229
00:43:08,525 --> 00:43:11,025
(They buy shaved pork belly instead of beef loin.)

1230
00:43:11,495 --> 00:43:13,364
Eun Ji, I found headscarves.

1231
00:43:13,365 --> 00:43:14,635
- Headscarves?
- Headscarves.

1232
00:43:15,265 --> 00:43:16,605
- We need to buy headscarves.
- Young Ji needs a headscarf.

1233
00:43:17,635 --> 00:43:19,635
- Two headscarves.
- Which colours should we get?

1234
00:43:21,275 --> 00:43:24,104
- The leopard print looks cute.
- Shall we get one leopard print?

1235
00:43:24,105 --> 00:43:25,845
- We need 1 of these.
- Let's get 1.

1236
00:43:26,445 --> 00:43:28,344
I'm sorry, but can I keep the leopard print?

1237
00:43:28,345 --> 00:43:29,345
Keep it.

1238
00:43:29,345 --> 00:43:30,345
(Smiling)

1239
00:43:30,346 --> 00:43:32,385
We got the headscarves.

1240
00:43:33,655 --> 00:43:36,015
What else can we buy here?

1241
00:43:36,885 --> 00:43:39,284
- We need kitchen scissors.
- We need kitchen scissors.

1242
00:43:39,285 --> 00:43:40,425
- Shall we get this?
- Yes.

1243
00:43:40,925 --> 00:43:41,954
Scissors.

1244
00:43:41,955 --> 00:43:43,495
(Everything on the supermarket list is purchased.)

1245
00:43:43,925 --> 00:43:44,994
(They have to head to the market to buy a big basin.)

1246
00:43:44,995 --> 00:43:47,195
- Take a look over here.
- Okay.

1247
00:43:47,435 --> 00:43:48,895
There are a lot of things here.

1248
00:43:49,295 --> 00:43:51,034
This is just like a fancy department store.

1249
00:43:51,035 --> 00:43:53,205
Eun Ji, this place is amazing.

1250
00:43:53,435 --> 00:43:55,234
- Yu Jin.
- I'm glad that we came shopping.

1251
00:43:55,235 --> 00:43:57,505
This is a fancy department store for us.

1252
00:43:58,205 --> 00:44:00,745
(They forget about grocery shopping and switch to shopping mode.)

1253
00:44:01,145 --> 00:44:02,984
- Look, Eun Ji.
- It's a strawberry.

1254
00:44:02,985 --> 00:44:06,044
- Yes, this is how it should be.
- Strawberry.

1255
00:44:06,045 --> 00:44:08,014
- I'll get the strawberry shape.
- I'll get the toast bread shape.

1256
00:44:08,015 --> 00:44:10,385
It's easier to scrub with.

1257
00:44:10,585 --> 00:44:11,855
- Like this?
- Like this.

1258
00:44:12,355 --> 00:44:13,925
I need a nail file.

1259
00:44:14,155 --> 00:44:15,895
- An eyebrow razor...
- And nail clippers.

1260
00:44:16,125 --> 00:44:17,795
- How about this?
- Who wants a tongue cleaner?

1261
00:44:18,465 --> 00:44:19,895
- I'll get one.
- It looks cute.

1262
00:44:20,295 --> 00:44:22,694
- Hygiene. What else?
- Maintaining hygiene.

1263
00:44:22,695 --> 00:44:24,665
I got so excited that I even threw my notebook.

1264
00:44:25,035 --> 00:44:26,735
- We need to go now.
- Let's go now.

1265
00:44:28,075 --> 00:44:29,775
Eun Ji, can't we get one?

1266
00:44:30,075 --> 00:44:31,944
- Let's buy one of the squishy toys.
- Can we?

1267
00:44:31,945 --> 00:44:33,914
- It's cute.
- Right? This is really...

1268
00:44:33,915 --> 00:44:35,714
It's a stress ball.

1269
00:44:35,715 --> 00:44:37,385
We need to keep our stress in check.

1270
00:44:37,885 --> 00:44:39,555
We really need this, Eun Ji.

1271
00:44:39,815 --> 00:44:41,284
For our mental health.

1272
00:44:41,285 --> 00:44:42,555
You agree with me, right?

1273
00:44:42,955 --> 00:44:44,054
You know how people say...

1274
00:44:44,055 --> 00:44:47,094
"A happy wife makes a happy home."

1275
00:44:47,095 --> 00:44:49,354
A happy chef in the kitchen...

1276
00:44:49,355 --> 00:44:51,395
makes a happy restaurant.

1277
00:44:52,425 --> 00:44:53,835
(Right on)

1278
00:44:53,865 --> 00:44:55,234
Okay. We're done here.

1279
00:44:55,235 --> 00:44:56,535
(Heading back with a heavy cart and a light wallet)

1280
00:44:57,135 --> 00:44:59,364
- We bought a lot of good stuff.
- Right. We bought a lot.

1281
00:44:59,365 --> 00:45:00,974
I got everything I wanted.

1282
00:45:00,975 --> 00:45:03,075
- We bought the scrubbers too.
- They really have everything there.

1283
00:45:03,505 --> 00:45:04,904
Hey, Yu Jin.

1284
00:45:04,905 --> 00:45:06,975
There's a lot of dishwashing items here.

1285
00:45:07,345 --> 00:45:09,244
We found another fancy department store.

1286
00:45:09,245 --> 00:45:11,745
- What should we do?
- I think we should visit there.

1287
00:45:12,185 --> 00:45:14,115
- Hello.
- Hello.

1288
00:45:14,385 --> 00:45:16,525
- Look at that, Eun Ji.
- Hello.

1289
00:45:17,025 --> 00:45:19,084
Yu Jin, this place is legendary.

1290
00:45:19,085 --> 00:45:21,155
- This is driving me crazy.
- We should've come here first.

1291
00:45:22,555 --> 00:45:24,494
Look, Yu Jin. We can sit here while doing the dishes.

1292
00:45:24,495 --> 00:45:25,524
Eun Ji.

1293
00:45:25,525 --> 00:45:27,235
I think we must buy this.

1294
00:45:27,595 --> 00:45:29,265
Go over there and try sitting on it.

1295
00:45:29,705 --> 00:45:30,705
How does it feel?

1296
00:45:30,706 --> 00:45:32,135
Will it be comfortable to sit there while doing the dishes?

1297
00:45:32,305 --> 00:45:34,204
Eun Ji, this is it.

1298
00:45:34,205 --> 00:45:36,074
Pretend you're doing the dishes and see how it feels.

1299
00:45:36,075 --> 00:45:37,205
(Pretending)

1300
00:45:38,475 --> 00:45:40,944
(She's posing perfectly as if she were doing the dishes.)

1301
00:45:40,945 --> 00:45:42,274
Was it inappropriate?

1302
00:45:42,275 --> 00:45:43,315
It's so good.

1303
00:45:43,715 --> 00:45:44,845
I really like it, Yu Jin.

1304
00:45:45,115 --> 00:45:47,014
Shall we get the largest, white one?

1305
00:45:47,015 --> 00:45:49,084
Please give us the largest one you have.

1306
00:45:49,085 --> 00:45:50,124
- This is...
- It's perfect.

1307
00:45:50,125 --> 00:45:52,425
- This is... Okay.
- It's perfect. Okay.

1308
00:45:52,995 --> 00:45:55,525
Where is it? I want to go check it out.

1309
00:45:56,365 --> 00:45:58,124
- Duwon-myeon.
- It's in Daejeon-ri.

1310
00:45:58,125 --> 00:45:59,264
- It's located by the sea.
- It's right by the sea.

1311
00:45:59,265 --> 00:46:00,594
- Daejeon-ri?
- Yes, Daejeon-ri.

1312
00:46:00,595 --> 00:46:01,964
- Yes.
- Daejeon-ri, Duwon-myeon?

1313
00:46:01,965 --> 00:46:03,805
- Please visit us soon.
- Okay.

1314
00:46:04,635 --> 00:46:05,764
- It's cold.
- Oh, dear. Eun Ji.

1315
00:46:05,765 --> 00:46:08,374
(They're done with grocery shopping!)

1316
00:46:08,375 --> 00:46:09,674
Let's start with jeolpyeon.

1317
00:46:09,675 --> 00:46:10,804
(Meanwhile, the kitchen team starts making rice cakes.)

1318
00:46:10,805 --> 00:46:11,875
Okay.

1319
00:46:12,875 --> 00:46:15,144
(Placing the baekseolgi that will transform into jeolpyeon)

1320
00:46:15,145 --> 00:46:16,215
- Hold on.
- I'll do it.

1321
00:46:17,045 --> 00:46:18,585
Look at that. It looks perfect.

1322
00:46:18,885 --> 00:46:21,254
(The baekseolgi is cooked to perfection.)

1323
00:46:21,255 --> 00:46:22,615
I'm glad we marked it earlier.

1324
00:46:22,855 --> 00:46:24,184
Here we go.

1325
00:46:24,185 --> 00:46:25,224
- Let's go.
- I'll...

1326
00:46:25,225 --> 00:46:26,724
I'll just do a quick test run and pull some out.

1327
00:46:26,725 --> 00:46:27,794
Okay.

1328
00:46:27,795 --> 00:46:30,324
(They get off to a smooth start, unexpectedly.)

1329
00:46:30,325 --> 00:46:32,525
(But...)

1330
00:46:35,995 --> 00:46:38,105
(The rice cake shaper won't even budge.)

1331
00:46:40,805 --> 00:46:42,405
Hey, what's wrong with you?

1332
00:46:42,775 --> 00:46:44,074
Director, why isn't this working?

1333
00:46:44,075 --> 00:46:45,375
- What's wrong?
- The rice cake won't come out.

1334
00:46:45,745 --> 00:46:47,845
(They hit a snag right from the beginning.)

1335
00:46:48,215 --> 00:46:49,545
Jebyeong, don't do this to us.

1336
00:46:50,385 --> 00:46:53,555
(She tries again calmly.)

1337
00:46:55,255 --> 00:46:57,154
- Oh, no. Stop.
- What is it?

1338
00:46:57,155 --> 00:46:58,885
Hold on. Stop the machine.

1339
00:46:59,055 --> 00:47:00,455
It's coming out from underneath.

1340
00:47:01,295 --> 00:47:03,025
Did something go wrong when we put it in?

1341
00:47:03,425 --> 00:47:04,464
Oh, you're right.

1342
00:47:04,465 --> 00:47:05,564
(Jeolpyeon is coming out squished from the wrong spot.)

1343
00:47:05,565 --> 00:47:06,565
It's coming out from underneath.

1344
00:47:06,795 --> 00:47:08,795
- I think we should reinstall it.
- Right.

1345
00:47:09,595 --> 00:47:11,134
(They struggle on their first try doing this on their own.)

1346
00:47:11,135 --> 00:47:12,305
This is driving me crazy.

1347
00:47:12,935 --> 00:47:15,135
- And then...
- Screw it in.

1348
00:47:15,375 --> 00:47:16,844
- Screw it in.
- Done.

1349
00:47:16,845 --> 00:47:18,174
- Okay. Let's try again.
- Done. Here we go.

1350
00:47:18,175 --> 00:47:20,344
- Here we go. I'll turn it on.
- Okay.

1351
00:47:20,345 --> 00:47:21,644
(The success of the business is on the line.)

1352
00:47:21,645 --> 00:47:23,714
- That's good. Great.
- It's working. What a relief.

1353
00:47:23,715 --> 00:47:25,214
Yes, that's good.

1354
00:47:25,215 --> 00:47:27,354
- Oh, gosh. I'll just pull it out.
- Pull it gently.

1355
00:47:27,355 --> 00:47:28,715
Okay. Go ahead.

1356
00:47:29,055 --> 00:47:30,954
- It's coming out nicely.
- Here we go.

1357
00:47:30,955 --> 00:47:32,455
I'm choked with emotion.

1358
00:47:33,055 --> 00:47:34,825
I feel like I'm going to cry.

1359
00:47:34,925 --> 00:47:36,154
I know, right?

1360
00:47:36,155 --> 00:47:37,695
I can't believe it's working.

1361
00:47:38,225 --> 00:47:39,265
I panicked.

1362
00:47:40,035 --> 00:47:41,694
- Okay. You can start stacking.
- It looks...

1363
00:47:41,695 --> 00:47:42,994
This is amazing.

1364
00:47:42,995 --> 00:47:45,004
- Young Ji, this is amazing.
- Good.

1365
00:47:45,005 --> 00:47:46,134
We're done with jeolpyeon.

1366
00:47:46,135 --> 00:47:47,435
- We're done with jeolpyeon.
- Yes, we're done.

1367
00:47:47,805 --> 00:47:50,175
- Garaetteok is a bigger challenge.
- I think I can stay positive.

1368
00:47:51,175 --> 00:47:52,605
That's good.

1369
00:47:52,975 --> 00:47:55,245
Nice. That's great.

1370
00:47:55,545 --> 00:47:57,385
Nice. Keep going.

1371
00:47:58,285 --> 00:47:59,285
(Stickiness, glossiness, thickness)

1372
00:47:59,286 --> 00:48:00,914
- This is crazy good.
- Nice. This is ridiculously good.

1373
00:48:00,915 --> 00:48:02,385
This is the best batch I've ever made.

1374
00:48:02,955 --> 00:48:04,424
- Great.
- I really did a good job.

1375
00:48:04,425 --> 00:48:05,454
(It looks like it came from a professional rice cake shop.)

1376
00:48:05,455 --> 00:48:06,525
This is insane.

1377
00:48:07,295 --> 00:48:09,965
(So garaetteok is piling up.)

1378
00:48:10,265 --> 00:48:12,364
Young Ji, this batch of garaetteok is just amazing.

1379
00:48:12,365 --> 00:48:13,594
Yes, that batch is amazing.

1380
00:48:13,595 --> 00:48:14,635
(They successfully made garaetteok as well.)

1381
00:48:14,765 --> 00:48:16,704
Look at this. It came out great.

1382
00:48:16,705 --> 00:48:18,465
Look here. One, two, three.

1383
00:48:20,605 --> 00:48:23,444
(She is touched.)

1384
00:48:23,445 --> 00:48:25,705
- Thank you.
- It came out really great.

1385
00:48:26,205 --> 00:48:27,214
Young Ji.

1386
00:48:27,215 --> 00:48:30,685
(But...)

1387
00:48:31,245 --> 00:48:34,255
(Raining)

1388
00:48:35,255 --> 00:48:36,355
Are you all right?

1389
00:48:37,385 --> 00:48:39,185
- It's raining. What do we do?
- Is this for real?

1390
00:48:39,285 --> 00:48:40,924
Mimi, it's pouring.

1391
00:48:40,925 --> 00:48:45,025
(It suddenly starts pouring.)

1392
00:48:45,365 --> 00:48:46,535
Are you all right?

1393
00:48:47,495 --> 00:48:49,035
- It's raining. What do we do?
- Is this for real?

1394
00:48:49,395 --> 00:48:50,904
Mimi, it's pouring.

1395
00:48:50,905 --> 00:48:55,105
(It suddenly starts pouring.)

1396
00:48:55,735 --> 00:48:56,904
Wait.

1397
00:48:56,905 --> 00:48:57,905
(The wind is blowing hard too.)

1398
00:48:58,445 --> 00:48:59,604
(Fluttering)

1399
00:48:59,605 --> 00:49:01,215
- I'm bringing water.
- Okay.

1400
00:49:01,415 --> 00:49:03,685
(The weather is looking ominous.)

1401
00:49:03,985 --> 00:49:07,885
(The rain and the wind are picking up.)

1402
00:49:09,785 --> 00:49:12,125
We haven't even opened our restaurant.

1403
00:49:13,395 --> 00:49:16,625
(The outdoor tables, before the restaurant is even open)

1404
00:49:17,525 --> 00:49:19,495
It's so humid today.

1405
00:49:19,865 --> 00:49:23,265
(It's humid in front of the restaurant.)

1406
00:49:24,405 --> 00:49:25,564
Oh, like this?

1407
00:49:25,565 --> 00:49:27,905
(The paper towel dreams of escaping.)

1408
00:49:28,305 --> 00:49:29,574
- Goodness. What's going on?
- I...

1409
00:49:29,575 --> 00:49:30,645
I lit a mosquito coil.

1410
00:49:30,875 --> 00:49:32,005
Should I light one more?

1411
00:49:32,245 --> 00:49:34,574
- The rice flour is...
- Oh, no.

1412
00:49:34,575 --> 00:49:36,274
- Are you all right?
- The wind is so strong.

1413
00:49:36,275 --> 00:49:37,984
- We will...
- Let's take a ten-minute break.

1414
00:49:37,985 --> 00:49:39,544
- Let's take a short break.
- Just for ten minutes.

1415
00:49:39,545 --> 00:49:41,684
- You two can go to your room...
- Okay.

1416
00:49:41,685 --> 00:49:42,955
- and rest for a while.
- Okay.

1417
00:49:43,525 --> 00:49:47,154
A screw fell out from the awning.

1418
00:49:47,155 --> 00:49:48,295
(The camera crew is packing up for now too.)

1419
00:49:48,455 --> 00:49:50,565
Mimi, stand there. I'll take a photo of you.

1420
00:49:50,765 --> 00:49:52,025
I just heard thunder.

1421
00:49:52,725 --> 00:49:54,694
- Young Ji.
- Mimi, say something, please.

1422
00:49:54,695 --> 00:49:56,835
- The rice cake we made...
- The kitchen is a mess now.

1423
00:49:57,305 --> 00:49:59,364
- Everything is...
- Guys, cover this...

1424
00:49:59,365 --> 00:50:01,375
- There's sauce or something in it.
- Oh, no. Gosh.

1425
00:50:02,775 --> 00:50:03,944
- Oh, goodness.
- Good.

1426
00:50:03,945 --> 00:50:05,174
Close the lid, at least. Yes.

1427
00:50:05,175 --> 00:50:08,415
Oh, no. Our kitchen is completely ruined.

1428
00:50:09,175 --> 00:50:10,585
Let's cover them with this.

1429
00:50:12,045 --> 00:50:16,455
(They cover the kitchenware with plastic sheet hastily.)

1430
00:50:23,765 --> 00:50:26,164
Who would come here for tteokbokki on a rainy day like this?

1431
00:50:26,165 --> 00:50:27,665
- Right. No one will come.
- That'd be crazy.

1432
00:50:31,505 --> 00:50:32,535
This is...

1433
00:50:40,375 --> 00:50:41,575
I'm so scared.

1434
00:50:41,675 --> 00:50:44,085
We might get an electric shock.

1435
00:50:45,415 --> 00:50:46,415
(They're worried about getting shocked on their grand opening day.)

1436
00:50:46,416 --> 00:50:48,614
This is our first day...

1437
00:50:48,615 --> 00:50:49,715
This is our first day here.

1438
00:50:50,385 --> 00:50:52,784
We just opened up the restaurant, and it's...

1439
00:50:52,785 --> 00:50:54,725
Look outside.

1440
00:50:55,195 --> 00:50:57,464
- Shall we go outside briefly?
- Okay.

1441
00:50:57,465 --> 00:50:58,624
- Just briefly?
- Okay.

1442
00:50:58,625 --> 00:50:59,695
Seriously.

1443
00:51:00,335 --> 00:51:01,535
I'm sorry.

1444
00:51:03,535 --> 00:51:04,805
Do you think anyone will come?

1445
00:51:05,335 --> 00:51:06,435
Will anyone come?

1446
00:51:08,775 --> 00:51:11,604
(Splashing)

1447
00:51:11,605 --> 00:51:12,644
No one can come in this rain.

1448
00:51:12,645 --> 00:51:14,845
I think our restaurant is doomed.

1449
00:51:16,475 --> 00:51:17,614
What should we do?

1450
00:51:17,615 --> 00:51:19,615
(The cloudy future)

1451
00:51:19,745 --> 00:51:22,155
We opened up a restaurant here!

1452
00:51:22,485 --> 00:51:23,984
Please come check it out!

1453
00:51:23,985 --> 00:51:26,054
Please come for tteokbokki!

1454
00:51:26,055 --> 00:51:28,155
Please come for tteokbokki.

1455
00:51:29,095 --> 00:51:31,024
We make our own rice cakes.

1456
00:51:31,025 --> 00:51:33,535
We made the rice cakes earlier today.

1457
00:51:34,465 --> 00:51:39,665
(Hollow eyes)

1458
00:51:40,605 --> 00:51:42,934
If it's just drizzling instead of pouring,

1459
00:51:42,935 --> 00:51:44,004
- we might have some customers.
- Exactly.

1460
00:51:44,005 --> 00:51:46,104
- I just heard thunder again.
- It's even thundering.

1461
00:51:46,105 --> 00:51:47,214
(Will they be able to open the restaurant today?)

1462
00:51:47,215 --> 00:51:49,314
- Then let's open it at 1pm.
- Okay.

1463
00:51:49,315 --> 00:51:51,615
We can take our time to prep everything.

1464
00:51:51,785 --> 00:51:52,985
- Let's have lunch too.
- Yes.

1465
00:51:53,655 --> 00:51:54,754
Let's drag it inside.

1466
00:51:54,755 --> 00:51:56,655
- Oh, I see.
- Let's move the whole thing.

1467
00:51:56,885 --> 00:52:00,524
(We are back, we are here)

1468
00:52:00,525 --> 00:52:01,994
(The food)

1469
00:52:01,995 --> 00:52:03,295
Gosh. Should we put this inside?

1470
00:52:04,495 --> 00:52:05,924
How should we do this efficiently?

1471
00:52:05,925 --> 00:52:06,964
(As the rain tapers off, they start preparing to open the restaurant.)

1472
00:52:06,965 --> 00:52:08,635
Let's put it aside.

1473
00:52:09,135 --> 00:52:12,205
(Meanwhile, these two are struggling to clean the rice cake machine.)

1474
00:52:12,335 --> 00:52:14,375
Gosh. Look at the rice cake wedged in here.

1475
00:52:15,305 --> 00:52:16,534
Seriously, rice cake...

1476
00:52:16,535 --> 00:52:17,604
(Filled with rice cake)

1477
00:52:17,605 --> 00:52:18,875
- It drives me crazy.
- Exactly.

1478
00:52:19,375 --> 00:52:21,145
Seriously, this is driving me crazy.

1479
00:52:23,715 --> 00:52:25,915
- But this... Wait. Eun Ji.
- Yes?

1480
00:52:25,985 --> 00:52:27,814
I think they made too many holes.

1481
00:52:27,815 --> 00:52:28,855
Why?

1482
00:52:29,385 --> 00:52:31,324
- I mean...
- We can't use this part.

1483
00:52:31,325 --> 00:52:33,024
- I'll go and complain about this.
- Right?

1484
00:52:33,025 --> 00:52:34,694
- We should complain about this.
- Hey.

1485
00:52:34,695 --> 00:52:35,755
We should complain about this.

1486
00:52:35,895 --> 00:52:37,464
Is there any way to prevent rice cake from being wedged?

1487
00:52:37,465 --> 00:52:38,625
- No. Right?
- No.

1488
00:52:38,895 --> 00:52:40,534
- Here...
- I can't complain to them.

1489
00:52:40,535 --> 00:52:41,794
- Okay. I'll do the rest.
- Right now...

1490
00:52:41,795 --> 00:52:42,795
They're already having a hard time.

1491
00:52:42,796 --> 00:52:43,835
- I can't say anything to them.
- Try shaking it.

1492
00:52:44,205 --> 00:52:46,105
(Watching them struggle touches a soft spot in their hearts.)

1493
00:52:46,365 --> 00:52:47,474
(Instead of complaining, they start cutting it out.)

1494
00:52:47,475 --> 00:52:49,005
