We're on the same team. We are the world.

1744
01:01:33,365 --> 01:01:35,094
(We are the world)

1745
01:01:35,095 --> 01:01:36,734
- Yes, we are...
- We are the children

1746
01:01:36,735 --> 01:01:38,134
We are the world,

1747
01:01:38,135 --> 01:01:40,364
but I'm so upset.

1748
01:01:40,365 --> 01:01:41,535
What should we do, then?

1749
01:01:41,905 --> 01:01:43,504
Let's all rise up.

1750
01:01:43,505 --> 01:01:45,275
(They go on strike.)

1751
01:01:45,645 --> 01:01:46,875
Get out before she comes back.

1752
01:01:47,675 --> 01:01:49,045
Get out before she comes back.

1753
01:01:50,145 --> 01:01:51,484
- She's outside.
- She's outside.

1754
01:01:51,485 --> 01:01:53,314
Hide here.

1755
01:01:53,315 --> 01:01:54,954
Come this way.

1756
01:01:54,955 --> 01:01:56,955
(Come this way!)

1757
01:01:57,425 --> 01:01:59,154
(They escape to the hall to avoid the roaming boss.)

1758
01:01:59,155 --> 01:02:00,285
Come here.

1759
01:02:02,695 --> 01:02:05,165
(A car passes by at that moment.)

1760
01:02:09,265 --> 01:02:11,364
Come and eat tteokbokki.

1761
01:02:11,365 --> 01:02:12,635
(She promotes the restaurant with an awkward smile.)

1762
01:02:13,265 --> 01:02:14,475
Come on!

1763
01:02:14,735 --> 01:02:16,405
He's so annoying.

1764
01:02:18,305 --> 01:02:19,575
I'm so mad.

1765
01:02:20,075 --> 01:02:21,145
She's here.

1766
01:02:21,445 --> 01:02:24,215
(Erasing her trace)

1767
01:02:24,845 --> 01:02:26,185
- What's this?
- She's here.

1768
01:02:27,185 --> 01:02:28,284
(Sighing)

1769
01:02:28,285 --> 01:02:29,315
What's this?

1770
01:02:29,615 --> 01:02:31,825
Where did they go?

1771
01:02:32,625 --> 01:02:33,625
Where...

1772
01:02:33,995 --> 01:02:37,295
(She sets off to find the employees.)

1773
01:02:37,465 --> 01:02:38,764
- This is...
- Right?

1774
01:02:38,765 --> 01:02:39,864
- Yes.
- Right?

1775
01:02:39,865 --> 01:02:41,364
- Yes.
- The business isn't doing well.

1776
01:02:41,365 --> 01:02:42,565
When will we...

1777
01:02:43,195 --> 01:02:44,565
The business isn't doing well,

1778
01:02:44,805 --> 01:02:46,104
she speaks so rudely,

1779
01:02:46,105 --> 01:02:47,505
and she hasn't paid us the wages yet.

1780
01:02:47,875 --> 01:02:48,875
She called her a thoughtless idol.

1781
01:02:48,876 --> 01:02:49,905
We prepared for seven hours.

1782
01:02:50,375 --> 01:02:52,074
- But there are no customers.
- We can't take pictures freely.

1783
01:02:52,075 --> 01:02:53,645
I can't take pictures freely when I'm an idol singer.

1784
01:02:54,345 --> 01:02:56,545
People, guys.

1785
01:02:58,385 --> 01:02:59,515
Ma'ams.

1786
01:03:04,455 --> 01:03:05,524
What is it?

1787
01:03:05,525 --> 01:03:07,795
- What are you doing?
- We're upset.

1788
01:03:08,195 --> 01:03:09,195
We won't work.

1789
01:03:10,795 --> 01:03:12,065
(Upset)

1790
01:03:12,465 --> 01:03:14,134
(The employees successfully teased the owner.)

1791
01:03:14,135 --> 01:03:15,335
She's upset.

1792
01:03:15,795 --> 01:03:18,705
(The owner's insides are burning.)

1793
01:03:18,865 --> 01:03:20,465
Come and have tteokbokki!

1794
01:03:21,775 --> 01:03:23,104
All she cares about is the business.

1795
01:03:23,105 --> 01:03:24,475
That's all she cares about.

1796
01:03:24,645 --> 01:03:25,744
All she cares about is the business.

1797
01:03:25,745 --> 01:03:27,945
All Mimi cares about is jeolpyeon.

1798
01:03:28,145 --> 01:03:29,414
All she cares about is the business.

1799
01:03:29,415 --> 01:03:30,645
- We've lost. Let's go.
- Okay.

1800
01:03:30,915 --> 01:03:31,945
Goodness.

1801
01:03:32,185 --> 01:03:34,185
Eat tteokbokki...

1802
01:03:35,755 --> 01:03:36,785
Hello.

1803
01:03:37,455 --> 01:03:38,524
Tteokbokki...

1804
01:03:38,525 --> 01:03:40,825
(An old lady becomes curious about the young owner's shouts.)

1805
01:03:40,995 --> 01:03:42,225
Hello.

1806
01:03:43,295 --> 01:03:45,125
(She feels awkward now that she's actually talking with one.)

1807
01:03:45,295 --> 01:03:46,625
We're selling tteokbokki.

1808
01:03:48,295 --> 01:03:49,735
Would you like to eat tteokbokki...

1809
01:03:51,005 --> 01:03:54,035
(The local senior's gesture makes her feel hopeless.)

1810
01:03:55,475 --> 01:03:57,205
Eat tteokbokki!

1811
01:03:58,305 --> 01:04:00,245
(Polite)

1812
01:04:01,475 --> 01:04:02,914
Eat tteokbokki.

1813
01:04:02,915 --> 01:04:04,385
(Hesitating)

1814
01:04:04,915 --> 01:04:05,915
They're running away.

1815
01:04:05,916 --> 01:04:07,085
(Running away)

1816
01:04:08,915 --> 01:04:09,915
Tteokbokki...

1817
01:04:10,755 --> 01:04:13,384
(She's practically chasing away the customers at this point.)

1818
01:04:13,385 --> 01:04:14,455
I...

1819
01:04:17,155 --> 01:04:18,395
Switch off the drone.

1820
01:04:19,195 --> 01:04:21,295
It isn't the time for this.

1821
01:04:22,465 --> 01:04:23,534
Tteokbokki...

1822
01:04:23,535 --> 01:04:26,065
(Seniors, she doesn't bite!)

1823
01:04:26,705 --> 01:04:27,705
Apologise.

1824
01:04:28,575 --> 01:04:30,205
(Employee 1: Apologise!)

1825
01:04:30,435 --> 01:04:32,745
- You're the worst.
- You're the worst.

1826
01:04:33,345 --> 01:04:34,415
Why?

1827
01:04:34,615 --> 01:04:36,974
I can't work if I'm getting this kind of treatment.

1828
01:04:36,975 --> 01:04:38,415
What should I do?

1829
01:04:38,815 --> 01:04:40,615
I tried to hitch hike just now.

1830
01:04:40,785 --> 01:04:42,354
Tteokbokki hitch hike!

1831
01:04:42,355 --> 01:04:45,755
We shouted at a grandma on a rooftop to come here too.

1832
01:04:46,985 --> 01:04:48,155
But you spent...

1833
01:04:48,425 --> 01:04:49,995
seven hours to prepare,

1834
01:04:50,725 --> 01:04:51,895
and we were called...

1835
01:04:52,495 --> 01:04:54,294
thoughtless idol singer and comedian.

1836
01:04:54,295 --> 01:04:56,065
We don't want to work like this.

1837
01:04:57,765 --> 01:05:00,635
You scolded us for not working when we just took a few pictures.

1838
01:05:01,405 --> 01:05:04,844
Heavy is the crown, as they say!

1839
01:05:04,845 --> 01:05:06,475
I'm just so frustrated!

1840
01:05:08,215 --> 01:05:10,275
This is my first time doing business as well.

1841
01:05:10,845 --> 01:05:11,915
And the woman...

1842
01:05:12,215 --> 01:05:14,584
in the kitchen is completely obsessed...

1843
01:05:14,585 --> 01:05:15,855
with rice cakes!

1844
01:05:16,155 --> 01:05:18,254
- All Kim Mi Hyun does...
- Only rice cakes...

1845
01:05:18,255 --> 01:05:19,725
is cut the jeolpyeon.

1846
01:05:19,985 --> 01:05:22,425
She doesn't make rice cakes, she only cuts them.

1847
01:05:23,325 --> 01:05:26,895
We didn't get any order, and she's made 12 servings!

1848
01:05:27,195 --> 01:05:30,735
My talented individuals, I beg of you.

1849
01:05:31,165 --> 01:05:33,505
Please attract at least one customer.

1850
01:05:33,635 --> 01:05:35,474
How can you touch the floor with the gloves on?

1851
01:05:35,475 --> 01:05:36,835
Throw the gloves away.

1852
01:05:37,175 --> 01:05:38,575
(Even during the discussion, hygiene is important.)

1853
01:05:38,775 --> 01:05:40,445
(They had a dramatic breakthrough. And she threw away the gloves.)

1854
01:05:41,115 --> 01:05:42,615
- We're off.
- Good luck.

1855
01:05:43,945 --> 01:05:45,045
I believe in you, Lee Eun Ji!

1856
01:05:45,345 --> 01:05:47,215
The best comedian in Korea!

1857
01:05:47,555 --> 01:05:50,885
The winner of the Baeksang Arts Awards! Please.

1858
01:05:51,485 --> 01:05:53,684
Please attract customers.

1859
01:05:53,685 --> 01:05:55,194
- Wait here.
- This won't do.

1860
01:05:55,195 --> 01:05:56,855
We need sky dancers.

1861
01:06:02,295 --> 01:06:03,794
Everyone, it's so nice to meet you.

1862
01:06:03,795 --> 01:06:06,005
Space Ride Cake has opened.

1863
01:06:06,235 --> 01:06:08,275
The head chef makes...

1864
01:06:08,475 --> 01:06:09,735
great tteokbokki,

1865
01:06:09,975 --> 01:06:13,204
assisted by the sous-chef.

1866
01:06:13,205 --> 01:06:15,545
Come to Space Rice Cake!

1867
01:06:15,775 --> 01:06:18,245
- You need to repeat after me.
- Come!

1868
01:06:18,745 --> 01:06:22,715
(They're pretty serious about this.)

1869
01:06:23,015 --> 01:06:24,154
Yu Jin.

1870
01:06:24,155 --> 01:06:26,354
There are seniors.

1871
01:06:26,355 --> 01:06:27,525
Shall we do it over there?

1872
01:06:28,155 --> 01:06:29,155
Let's do it one more time over there.

1873
01:06:29,595 --> 01:06:31,095
When I say "come," you say "come."

1874
01:06:31,595 --> 01:06:33,324
- When I say "find," say "find."
- Find!

1875
01:06:33,325 --> 01:06:35,265
- When I say "love," say "love."
- Love!

1876
01:06:35,935 --> 01:06:37,964
It's a bit embarrassing. How will I do this?

1877
01:06:37,965 --> 01:06:39,964
- Yu Jin, step up here.
- Come on, Eun Ji.

1878
01:06:39,965 --> 01:06:42,404
Do it! Aren't you going to attract customers?

1879
01:06:42,405 --> 01:06:43,405
A car.

1880
01:06:43,406 --> 01:06:44,444
(Rushing)

1881
01:06:44,445 --> 01:06:46,104
A car is coming. Yu Jin, stand here.

1882
01:06:46,105 --> 01:06:47,475
(The employees get busy at the appearance of a luxury car.)

1883
01:06:47,845 --> 01:06:49,875
(They solemnly play a song.)

1884
01:06:50,315 --> 01:06:51,585
Are you ready... Put your hand on my shoulder.

1885
01:06:52,945 --> 01:06:54,485
Move your hips to the left first. Seven, eight.

1886
01:06:55,615 --> 01:06:57,455
Everyone, it's so nice to meet you.

1887
01:06:57,625 --> 01:06:59,024
We're Space Rice Cake.

1888
01:06:59,025 --> 01:07:01,654
Please show lots of love for the newly-opened restaurant!

1889
01:07:01,655 --> 01:07:02,724
Love!

1890
01:07:02,725 --> 01:07:05,795
Space Rice Cake has an amazing head chef.

1891
01:07:06,065 --> 01:07:07,734
Head chef is Lee Young Ji,

1892
01:07:07,735 --> 01:07:10,464
and Kim Mi Hyun makes desserts.

1893
01:07:10,465 --> 01:07:12,935
- Please support us!
- Support!

1894
01:07:13,665 --> 01:07:15,935
(Sure, good luck.)

1895
01:07:17,805 --> 01:07:20,444
Eun Ji, I said it was embarrassing.

1896
01:07:20,445 --> 01:07:21,674
Wait, who's laughing?

1897
01:07:21,675 --> 01:07:22,745
Don't mock us!

1898
01:07:23,975 --> 01:07:26,744
(She's very angry at the headquarter's mocking.)

1899
01:07:26,745 --> 01:07:27,815
Darn it.

1900
01:07:28,385 --> 01:07:29,414
Eun Ji.

1901
01:07:29,415 --> 01:07:31,684
Why didn't the word about our business spread?

1902
01:07:31,685 --> 01:07:33,125
Don't mock us.

1903
01:07:33,525 --> 01:07:34,925
- Mimi.
- Yes.

1904
01:07:35,495 --> 01:07:38,165
(While the salespeople are struggling)

1905
01:07:38,425 --> 01:07:40,325
- What are you doing?
- Cutting rice cakes.

1906
01:07:42,065 --> 01:07:44,034
- Boss.
- They're on strike.

1907
01:07:44,035 --> 01:07:46,604
- Head Chef.
- Yes.

1908
01:07:46,605 --> 01:07:49,404
Why do you get mad on your own...

1909
01:07:49,405 --> 01:07:51,404
and beg on your own?

1910
01:07:51,405 --> 01:07:52,405
We should teach the Gen Z a lesson.

1911
01:07:52,406 --> 01:07:54,714
I had to beg. Am I the strange one here?

1912
01:07:54,715 --> 01:07:57,114
I'm the head chef and the owner.

1913
01:07:57,115 --> 01:07:58,144
But I...

1914
01:07:58,145 --> 01:08:00,344
I just scolded them for taking pictures during the opening hours.

1915
01:08:00,345 --> 01:08:02,614
Am I the strange one? Am I the boomer?

1916
01:08:02,615 --> 01:08:04,154
Mimi, am I the strange one?

1917
01:08:04,155 --> 01:08:05,984
Stop cutting rice cakes and say something.

1918
01:08:05,985 --> 01:08:07,085
You're not Han Seok Bong.

1919
01:08:07,655 --> 01:08:10,455
Stop cutting rice cakes and speak. Am I the strange one?

1920
01:08:10,925 --> 01:08:13,465
They're slacking during working hours.

1921
01:08:13,695 --> 01:08:15,235
Am I wrong for telling them off?

1922
01:08:15,695 --> 01:08:18,235
They say I'm wrong and that I should apologise.

1923
01:08:18,305 --> 01:08:19,334
(The owner is so close to fainting from anger.)

1924
01:08:19,335 --> 01:08:20,335
They want me to apologise.

1925
01:08:20,705 --> 01:08:21,734
Catch them.

1926
01:08:21,735 --> 01:08:23,605
(Catch the employees.)

1927
01:08:23,875 --> 01:08:25,344
Let's go with this, then.

1928
01:08:25,345 --> 01:08:26,875
- Like this.
- Okay?

1929
01:08:29,475 --> 01:08:31,185
Don't stare too much at the raw fish restaurant.

1930
01:08:33,045 --> 01:08:34,984
(Aggressive promotion in front of the competitor)

1931
01:08:34,985 --> 01:08:37,754
Space Rice Cake has opened.

1932
01:08:37,755 --> 01:08:40,954
The rice cake is very delicious. Please show lots of love!

1933
01:08:40,955 --> 01:08:41,995
Love!

1934
01:08:44,195 --> 01:08:45,225
Ha!

1935
01:08:45,695 --> 01:08:46,725
Come on, Yu Jin.

1936
01:08:48,035 --> 01:08:49,834
Eun Ji.

1937
01:08:49,835 --> 01:08:51,565
I can't do this.

1938
01:08:52,935 --> 01:08:54,165
- Mimi...
- Yes?

1939
01:08:54,905 --> 01:08:55,905
Yes?

1940
01:08:56,635 --> 01:08:58,645
- Eun Ji!
- Why is she running away?

1941
01:08:58,905 --> 01:08:59,905
Why is she...

1942
01:09:00,375 --> 01:09:01,575
running away from me?

1943
01:09:02,145 --> 01:09:04,414
Mimi is still cutting rice cakes.

1944
01:09:04,415 --> 01:09:06,645
What? That woman is...

1945
01:09:06,745 --> 01:09:08,384
possessed by a rice cake spirit.

1946
01:09:08,385 --> 01:09:10,684
Wear your aprons. You must be cold.

1947
01:09:10,685 --> 01:09:12,154
- Love us.
- I love you guys.

1948
01:09:12,155 --> 01:09:14,284
- Put it on me.
- What kind of...

1949
01:09:14,285 --> 01:09:16,895
- What kind of idol singer am I?
- A sexy one.

1950
01:09:17,925 --> 01:09:18,965
(Satisfied with the compliment)

1951
01:09:19,125 --> 01:09:20,395
A sexy idol singer.

1952
01:09:20,925 --> 01:09:22,335
- And?
- A cute one.

1953
01:09:23,595 --> 01:09:24,605
A cute idol singer.

1954
01:09:24,735 --> 01:09:26,505
Gosh, those guys.

1955
01:09:27,705 --> 01:09:30,234
They're so ungrateful.

1956
01:09:30,235 --> 01:09:31,245
(Seok Bong's mother is frustrated too.)

1957
01:09:31,745 --> 01:09:34,444
This mess happened because the head chef left her post.

1958
01:09:34,445 --> 01:09:35,475
Don't you think?

1959
01:09:35,875 --> 01:09:38,244
- Mi Hyun.
- Come back and secure your spot!

1960
01:09:38,245 --> 01:09:41,385
I... Earlier, you told me to get the employees back.

1961
01:09:42,055 --> 01:09:43,655
What do you want me to do?

1962
01:09:44,285 --> 01:09:46,055
Is the head chef a punching bag?

1963
01:09:47,325 --> 01:09:48,355
What should I do?

1964
01:09:49,425 --> 01:09:51,665
Mimi, you told me to go and catch them.

1965
01:09:52,465 --> 01:09:53,525
What am I...

1966
01:09:53,965 --> 01:09:57,265
You're treating me like a head minion, not a head chef.

1967
01:09:57,535 --> 01:09:59,005
What's this?

1968
01:09:59,835 --> 01:10:02,905
Mimi, they say you're crazy.

1969
01:10:03,875 --> 01:10:06,445
They call you crazy for cutting rice cakes when there's no order.

1970
01:10:07,675 --> 01:10:09,774
- A human should be a bit crazy.
- Let's wash our feet outside.

1971
01:10:09,775 --> 01:10:10,975
Okay, let's.

1972
01:10:12,815 --> 01:10:14,485
And tear the recipe book.

1973
01:10:15,785 --> 01:10:17,884
There's no customer. What will we do?

1974
01:10:17,885 --> 01:10:19,055
I don't know.

1975
01:10:20,055 --> 01:10:21,355
Do you like rice cakes, ma'am?

1976
01:10:21,455 --> 01:10:23,255
(The salespeople are asking her a loaded question.)

1977
01:10:23,455 --> 01:10:26,295
- I do eat rice cakes.
- You do? Which is your favourite?

1978
01:10:28,165 --> 01:10:29,194
I like garaetteok.

1979
01:10:29,195 --> 01:10:31,664
- Would you like some garaetteok?
- Let me give you a taste of it.

1980
01:10:31,665 --> 01:10:32,965
- I'll bring it for you.
- Please wait. We'll bring it.

1981
01:10:33,435 --> 01:10:34,634
(Running to find garaetteok, which can be found so easily)

1982
01:10:34,635 --> 01:10:36,975
- Young Ji!
- Wrap it in dried gopchang laver.

1983
01:10:37,605 --> 01:10:39,205
(The old lady says something.)

1984
01:10:41,475 --> 01:10:43,415
You're coming to eat our food?

1985
01:10:45,545 --> 01:10:46,714
I'll go now if that's what you want.

1986
01:10:46,715 --> 01:10:48,214
No, a bit later.

1987
01:10:48,215 --> 01:10:49,755
Go take care of your business.

1988
01:10:50,085 --> 01:10:51,355
Come if you can.

1989
01:10:51,925 --> 01:10:52,985
Thank you.

1990
01:10:55,225 --> 01:10:57,925
- Young Ji.
- Yes.

1991
01:10:58,325 --> 01:11:00,025
We got a reservation.

1992
01:11:00,465 --> 01:11:02,265
(Out of office)

1993
01:11:02,735 --> 01:11:04,635
- Where are you, Young Ji?
- Where is she?

1994
01:11:04,905 --> 01:11:05,965
A reservation?

1995
01:11:06,135 --> 01:11:07,835
Go to the kitchen quickly!

1996
01:11:08,675 --> 01:11:10,175
Mimi, we got an order!

1997
01:11:10,405 --> 01:11:11,604
Goodness.

1998
01:11:11,605 --> 01:11:13,544
(She calls Seok Bong Mimi, who was taking a breather.)

1999
01:11:13,545 --> 01:11:15,514
We got a reservation. Let's go.

2000
01:11:15,515 --> 01:11:16,874
(They pick up the pace to the kitchen.)

2001
01:11:16,875 --> 01:11:17,915
What do you mean?

2002
01:11:17,985 --> 01:11:20,245
- See? They succeeded.
- What?

2003
01:11:21,155 --> 01:11:23,085
- What?
- Mi Hyun. Sous-chef.

