2258
01:20:15,985 --> 01:20:17,315
Are you all right?

2259
01:20:18,855 --> 01:20:20,084
- Is it okay to step inside?
- It was just...

2260
01:20:20,085 --> 01:20:21,654
Yes, you can come in.

2261
01:20:21,655 --> 01:20:23,095
- It's so scary.
- It's nothing.

2262
01:20:23,325 --> 01:20:25,024
(Actually, a special secret...)

2263
01:20:25,025 --> 01:20:27,264
(is hidden in Young Ji's tteokbokki.)

2264
01:20:27,265 --> 01:20:29,695
(It's time!)

2265
01:20:29,865 --> 01:20:30,894
It looks ready.

2266
01:20:30,895 --> 01:20:34,465
No. You shouldn't think that it's ready.

2267
01:20:34,965 --> 01:20:36,275
- Then it doesn't taste right.
- No.

2268
01:20:36,335 --> 01:20:37,375
I know what you're saying.

2269
01:20:38,105 --> 01:20:41,075
(For garaetteok to absorb the sauce,)

2270
01:20:41,845 --> 01:20:43,844
It'll be ready in ten minutes.

2271
01:20:43,845 --> 01:20:45,785
(it'll take 10 minutes!)

2272
01:20:46,215 --> 01:20:47,644
I'm excited to cook.

2273
01:20:47,645 --> 01:20:49,485
I'm happy. I love you all.

2274
01:20:49,655 --> 01:20:51,784
(Current progress of tteokbokki)

2275
01:20:51,785 --> 01:20:53,955
(Original: 50 percent, Mala: 0 percent)

2276
01:20:54,085 --> 01:20:56,324
Now, I'll make the ghost pepper tteokbokki.

2277
01:20:56,325 --> 01:20:57,695
(Only now, she starts to make the second dish.)

2278
01:20:57,825 --> 01:21:01,464
Did you hear we have an order of a medium original tteokbokki too?

2279
01:21:01,465 --> 01:21:03,594
I didn't hear about the additional order.

2280
01:21:03,595 --> 01:21:04,895
I'm hearing this for the first time.

2281
01:21:05,505 --> 01:21:07,235
- There's an additional order.
- Okay.

2282
01:21:09,605 --> 01:21:10,975
I feel good right now.

2283
01:21:11,305 --> 01:21:13,344
Who is this guy?

2284
01:21:13,345 --> 01:21:14,405
He's my nephew.

2285
01:21:14,575 --> 01:21:16,375
He's Mi Suk's son.

2286
01:21:17,345 --> 01:21:19,615
- You should've told me.
- What a handsome guy.

2287
01:21:20,085 --> 01:21:22,054
- He looks so much like her.
- He's handsome.

2288
01:21:22,055 --> 01:21:23,785
- So I was going to ask.
- Exactly.

2289
01:21:24,285 --> 01:21:25,724
He is such a good son.

2290
01:21:25,725 --> 01:21:27,225
- He's good-looking.
- Yes.

2291
01:21:27,255 --> 01:21:29,024
What is your mom doing?

2292
01:21:29,025 --> 01:21:30,055
She's coming.

2293
01:21:30,495 --> 01:21:31,554
- I see.
- We came separately.

2294
01:21:31,555 --> 01:21:33,995
(Actually, Mi Suk is coming right in.)

2295
01:21:36,765 --> 01:21:38,235
Welcome.

2296
01:21:38,505 --> 01:21:40,505
Yes. You can go inside.

2297
01:21:40,665 --> 01:21:41,834
There are customers here,

2298
01:21:41,835 --> 01:21:43,134
- so do you want to go to...
- Come in.

2299
01:21:43,135 --> 01:21:45,605
Is she your friend, sir? Please go inside.

2300
01:21:46,105 --> 01:21:48,374
The village chief is...

2301
01:21:48,375 --> 01:21:49,414
- amazing.
- Is he a superstar?

2302
01:21:49,415 --> 01:21:51,314
We have another table because of him.

2303
01:21:51,315 --> 01:21:53,244
- The village chief is awesome.
- He's amazing.

2304
01:21:53,245 --> 01:21:55,514
He is like...

2305
01:21:55,515 --> 01:21:56,915
George Clooney.

2306
01:21:57,255 --> 01:21:58,854
- That amazing?
- "Let's do it."

2307
01:21:58,855 --> 01:21:59,855
- Nice.
- Young Ji.

2308
01:21:59,856 --> 01:22:01,655
- It looks so good.
- It's really tasty.

2309
01:22:02,195 --> 01:22:04,895
(When the first tteokbokki starts to simmer,)

2310
01:22:05,395 --> 01:22:08,595
(she adds mini sausages right away.)

2311
01:22:08,995 --> 01:22:11,095
(When the fryer reaches the right temperature,)

2312
01:22:11,395 --> 01:22:12,404
Okay.

2313
01:22:12,405 --> 01:22:13,734
(shrimp, cod, and cuttlefish go in.)

2314
01:22:13,735 --> 01:22:15,105
I'm starting to fry them.

2315
01:22:16,575 --> 01:22:18,805
(After setting the timer,)

2316
01:22:19,805 --> 01:22:20,904
(she moves it up and down so that they don't stick together.)

2317
01:22:20,905 --> 01:22:23,244
- Let's go.
- Let's go. We can do it.

2318
01:22:23,245 --> 01:22:25,585
- Yes. Tteokbokki looks good today.
- Yes.

2319
01:22:27,785 --> 01:22:29,985
(Moving a long way to start making the pasta)

2320
01:22:30,185 --> 01:22:31,484
We'll get started quickly.

2321
01:22:31,485 --> 01:22:33,325
(She turns on the heat first.)

2322
01:22:33,885 --> 01:22:36,254
(She starts...)

2323
01:22:36,255 --> 01:22:38,925
(by adding minced garlic to olive oil.)

2324
01:22:39,265 --> 01:22:41,834
(After sautéing it for a while...)

2325
01:22:41,835 --> 01:22:43,564
Mimi, one minute left on the fryer.

2326
01:22:43,565 --> 01:22:44,934
- Okay.
- It's for one small original.

2327
01:22:44,935 --> 01:22:45,964
Okay.

2328
01:22:45,965 --> 01:22:47,505
(She goes back to finish the fritters.)

2329
01:22:47,965 --> 01:22:51,805
(She takes out the crunchy fritters.)

2330
01:22:54,145 --> 01:22:55,975
They look good.

2331
01:22:57,375 --> 01:22:58,745
I'll add the fritters now.

2332
01:22:58,815 --> 01:23:00,284
Okay. Add them.

2333
01:23:00,285 --> 01:23:01,285
(Cuttlefish)

2334
01:23:01,286 --> 01:23:02,454
(Shrimp)

2335
01:23:02,455 --> 01:23:04,615
(Cod)

2336
01:23:05,085 --> 01:23:07,854
(Lastly, she adds scallions...)

2337
01:23:07,855 --> 01:23:08,855
(and sesame seeds to finish.)

2338
01:23:08,856 --> 01:23:10,994
Eun Ji, a small original tteokbokki is ready to be served.

2339
01:23:10,995 --> 01:23:12,895
(Finishing in 10 minutes)

2340
01:23:13,125 --> 01:23:14,394
- Is it this one?
- Yes.

2341
01:23:14,395 --> 01:23:16,495
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

2342
01:23:17,195 --> 01:23:19,004
Here's the small original tteokbokki.

2343
01:23:19,005 --> 01:23:20,834
- Nice.
- Here it is.

2344
01:23:20,835 --> 01:23:21,935
(Don't Eat Ghost Pepper Tteokbokki, pollack roe and clam pasta)

2345
01:23:23,135 --> 01:23:24,204
Hurry and eat it.

2346
01:23:24,205 --> 01:23:26,474
It's big. Is it supposed to be served like this?

2347
01:23:26,475 --> 01:23:29,115
It's huge tteokbokki.

2348
01:23:30,045 --> 01:23:32,645
(The old lady tries a bite first.)

2349
01:23:33,145 --> 01:23:34,584
(And the village chief's family tries it too.)

2350
01:23:34,585 --> 01:23:35,685
Why aren't you eating that?

2351
01:23:36,015 --> 01:23:37,155
(Savouring)

2352
01:23:37,285 --> 01:23:38,385
It's tasty.

2353
01:23:38,955 --> 01:23:40,955
- Is it tasty?
- What?

2354
01:23:41,125 --> 01:23:42,824
- Yes, it's tasty.
- Does tteokbokki taste good?

2355
01:23:42,825 --> 01:23:43,855
Yes.

2356
01:23:44,155 --> 01:23:45,665
Goodness. This is so tasty too.

2357
01:23:45,725 --> 01:23:47,894
- This is tasty too.
- Dongchimi is tasty.

2358
01:23:47,895 --> 01:23:48,895
- Yes.
- Yes.

2359
01:23:48,965 --> 01:23:51,235
(Slurping)

2360
01:23:51,735 --> 01:23:54,935
(A mysterious shade appears in the meantime.)

2361
01:23:55,205 --> 01:23:56,275
It's good.

2362
01:23:56,475 --> 01:23:57,875
Goodness. This is so tasty too.

2363
01:24:00,175 --> 01:24:01,245
Do they find it tasty?

2364
01:24:03,575 --> 01:24:04,715
They said it was tasty.

2365
01:24:05,075 --> 01:24:06,084
Really? I'm happy to hear that.

2366
01:24:06,085 --> 01:24:07,285
- They said it was good.
- Thank you.

2367
01:24:07,385 --> 01:24:08,555
They say it's tasty.

2368
01:24:08,685 --> 01:24:10,085
That's nice.

2369
01:24:11,155 --> 01:24:13,925
(Reason: Ghost Paper Tteokbokki needs to be made ASAP)

2370
01:24:14,355 --> 01:24:15,724
(Adding chilli bean sauce to add the mala flavour)

2371
01:24:15,725 --> 01:24:17,025
I'll add 1.5 spoonfuls.

2372
01:24:18,595 --> 01:24:21,895
(Adding the spicy tang with the Sichuan pepper oil)

2373
01:24:23,365 --> 01:24:25,965
(Even the ghost pepper powder too!)

2374
01:24:26,105 --> 01:24:27,105
Seventeen minutes.

2375
01:24:27,665 --> 01:24:29,235
Garaetteok is added.

2376
01:24:29,535 --> 01:24:30,805
Okay.

2377
01:24:31,775 --> 01:24:35,415
(And she keeps simmering it down.)

2378
01:24:35,945 --> 01:24:38,644
(Something looks missing.)

2379
01:24:38,645 --> 01:24:40,244
(It's because...)

2380
01:24:40,245 --> 01:24:42,155
(it's missing the beef loin.)

2381
01:24:42,885 --> 01:24:45,084
(Remember me.)

2382
01:24:45,085 --> 01:24:46,554
(Current status of tteokbokki)

2383
01:24:46,555 --> 01:24:48,055
(Missing beef loin)

2384
01:24:48,595 --> 01:24:51,355
(But the chef hasn't realised it.)

2385
01:24:51,925 --> 01:24:53,765
Young Ji, what about the beef loin?

2386
01:24:55,065 --> 01:24:56,065
That's right.

2387
01:24:57,365 --> 01:24:58,395
- Hold on.
- Okay.

2388
01:25:00,605 --> 01:25:01,605
(Sighing)

2389
01:25:01,935 --> 01:25:04,074
(She looks for the beef loin in a hurry.)

2390
01:25:04,075 --> 01:25:05,105
This is crazy.

2391
01:25:06,005 --> 01:25:07,574
It's okay, Chef.

2392
01:25:07,575 --> 01:25:09,574
- I'm working on it.
- We have enough time.

2393
01:25:09,575 --> 01:25:11,015
It's okay.

2394
01:25:11,245 --> 01:25:13,644
(Finally adding the beef loin)

2395
01:25:13,645 --> 01:25:15,245
It's all good.

2396
01:25:15,785 --> 01:25:17,885
(While she tries to fix her mistake in a hurry,)

2397
01:25:18,355 --> 01:25:21,725
(another tteokbokki is left without the rice cake.)

2398
01:25:21,995 --> 01:25:23,554
- Is that...
- It's the original tteokbokki.

2399
01:25:23,555 --> 01:25:24,894
I see. The original.

2400
01:25:24,895 --> 01:25:26,625
They'll serve the same thing for us.

2401
01:25:27,625 --> 01:25:29,535
Don't Eat Ghost Pepper Tteokbokki is ready.

2402
01:25:29,965 --> 01:25:31,264
Ghost Pepper is ready.

2403
01:25:31,265 --> 01:25:32,904
- Okay.
- Okay. I'm coming.

2404
01:25:32,905 --> 01:25:34,135
Come, Monkfish.

2405
01:25:34,205 --> 01:25:36,075
Good job. You're generous.

2406
01:25:36,435 --> 01:25:38,674
(Tteokbokki is simmering without rice cake.)

2407
01:25:38,675 --> 01:25:39,775
I'll take it.

2408
01:25:40,105 --> 01:25:41,545
- It's over here.
- I see.

2409
01:25:41,605 --> 01:25:43,114
(Current status of tteokbokki)

2410
01:25:43,115 --> 01:25:44,545
(Missing rice cakes)

2411
01:25:45,045 --> 01:25:46,114
Hello.

2412
01:25:46,115 --> 01:25:47,145
(Here comes the Ghost Pepper Tteokbokki.)

2413
01:25:47,845 --> 01:25:50,414
(They make room on their table.)

2414
01:25:50,415 --> 01:25:52,355
- Here's the spicy one.
- It's...

2415
01:25:53,025 --> 01:25:54,085
Is it the mala one?

2416
01:25:54,155 --> 01:25:55,355
Why do you serve us only?

2417
01:25:56,355 --> 01:25:58,124
(Sadly, the tteokbokki is for the village chief's table.)

2418
01:25:58,125 --> 01:25:59,965
I didn't eat anything in the morning.

2419
01:26:00,525 --> 01:26:02,164
(She adds rice cake for the head of the women's association.)

2420
01:26:02,165 --> 01:26:04,395
- I added rice cake.
- Okay. Thank you.

2421
01:26:05,235 --> 01:26:07,305
(Now, it has to simmer for 10 minutes.)

2422
01:26:07,965 --> 01:26:10,405
(Rice cake has returned.)

2423
01:26:11,535 --> 01:26:13,245
- Why isn't ours coming?
- Right, sir.

2424
01:26:14,045 --> 01:26:15,104
(Right, sir.)

2425
01:26:15,105 --> 01:26:16,674
It's coming right away.

2426
01:26:16,675 --> 01:26:18,645
Our head chef is taking care of it all the time.

2427
01:26:19,045 --> 01:26:20,214
Please give us a minute.

2428
01:26:20,215 --> 01:26:22,584
Because it's our first day,

2429
01:26:22,585 --> 01:26:23,815
the head chef is all over the place.

2430
01:26:24,085 --> 01:26:25,624
We'll come back with it quickly.

2431
01:26:25,625 --> 01:26:26,625
- Okay.
- Yes.

2432
01:26:26,626 --> 01:26:28,284
People on Table Two said,

2433
01:26:28,285 --> 01:26:30,454
"Why isn't our food coming?"

2434
01:26:30,455 --> 01:26:31,694
- I see.
- Sorry.

2435
01:26:31,695 --> 01:26:33,024
I'll make it over here.

2436
01:26:33,025 --> 01:26:35,664
(The kitchen team is in chaos.)

2437
01:26:35,665 --> 01:26:37,194
- Yes.
- A comment from Table Two.

2438
01:26:37,195 --> 01:26:38,364
- I'll get on with it.
- Okay.

2439
01:26:38,365 --> 01:26:39,605
(The service team is stressed from both sides.)

2440
01:26:40,235 --> 01:26:42,974
(While Young Ji is in a hurry,)

2441
01:26:42,975 --> 01:26:46,345
(it'll take a while for it to simmer down.)

2442
01:26:46,575 --> 01:26:48,645
We'll get the original tteokbokki...

2443
01:26:48,845 --> 01:26:50,145
and the pollack roe and clam pasta.

2444
01:26:50,315 --> 01:26:51,844
Would the two be it? Okay.

2445
01:26:51,845 --> 01:26:52,915
Here.

2446
01:26:52,985 --> 01:26:55,785
One medium original tteokbokki and a pollack roe and clam pasta.

2447
01:26:55,985 --> 01:26:57,084
And a pomegranate slushy.

2448
01:26:57,085 --> 01:26:58,284
The previous order of medium original tteokbokki...

2449
01:26:58,285 --> 01:26:59,454
hasn't been served.

2450
01:26:59,455 --> 01:27:01,084
- It hasn't.
- It's a different order, right?

2451
01:27:01,085 --> 01:27:02,325
- That's right.
- Got it.

2452
01:27:02,755 --> 01:27:03,994
Give it a try.

2453
01:27:03,995 --> 01:27:05,324
(They are sharing food in the hall.)

2454
01:27:05,325 --> 01:27:07,165
- Don't give it to us.
- Ours is coming soon.

2455
01:27:07,365 --> 01:27:08,695
For goodness' sake.

2456
01:27:09,535 --> 01:27:12,565
(Putting out the fire for now)

2457
01:27:12,835 --> 01:27:14,065
Excuse me.

2458
01:27:14,505 --> 01:27:17,104
Do you want to keep it warm?

2459
01:27:17,105 --> 01:27:18,335
We have a portable burner.

2460
01:27:18,745 --> 01:27:19,944
- We can bring it.
- It's still hot.

2461
01:27:19,945 --> 01:27:20,945
- It's okay.
- Is it okay?

2462
01:27:20,946 --> 01:27:22,544
Okay. Let me know if you need it.

2463
01:27:22,545 --> 01:27:23,545
- Okay.
- Yes.

2464
01:27:23,546 --> 01:27:25,175
(She saw how they shared food.)

2465
01:27:25,445 --> 01:27:27,285
The customers at Table Two...

2466
01:27:27,545 --> 01:27:29,915
are having tteokbokki shared by the table next to them.

2467
01:27:30,715 --> 01:27:32,824
- I'll hurry. Sorry.
- Sorry.

2468
01:27:32,825 --> 01:27:34,825
(It doesn't go smoothly as she planned.)

2469
01:27:36,695 --> 01:27:37,695
Oh, dear.

2470
01:27:37,925 --> 01:27:40,024
(While we wait for the tteokbokki,)

2471
01:27:40,025 --> 01:27:42,895
(I'll make the clam pasta.)

2472
01:27:43,895 --> 01:27:45,734
(Orders from the village chief's and Mi Suk's tables)

2473
01:27:45,735 --> 01:27:47,405
(Pollack roe and clam pasta)

2474
01:27:47,935 --> 01:27:49,734
(A little bit of water)

2475
01:27:49,735 --> 01:27:51,635
(A little bit of the chicken stock)

2476
01:27:52,645 --> 01:27:53,804
(Add a cup of clams.)

2477
01:27:53,805 --> 01:27:55,105
I added the ingredients.

2478
01:27:56,375 --> 01:27:59,414
(She also adds a generous amount of jeolpyeon.)

2479
01:27:59,415 --> 01:28:01,285
(Then she stir-fries them.)

2480
01:28:01,715 --> 01:28:02,884
(Adding a piece of butter...)

2481
01:28:02,885 --> 01:28:05,085
(and two spoonfuls of pollock roe)

2482
01:28:05,485 --> 01:28:08,425
(After stir-frying them until her face becomes red,)

2483
01:28:09,455 --> 01:28:12,625
(the pollock roe covers the jeolpyeon perfectly.)

2484
01:28:12,765 --> 01:28:14,165
We're ready to serve it.

2485
01:28:15,225 --> 01:28:16,764
(Village chief's table)

2486
01:28:16,765 --> 01:28:18,765
(Pollack roe and clam pasta)

2487
01:28:19,205 --> 01:28:21,164
(Mi Suk's table)

2488
01:28:21,165 --> 01:28:23,675
(Pollack roe and clam pasta)

2489
01:28:24,635 --> 01:28:27,045
It wasn't easy to make these.

2490
01:28:27,275 --> 01:28:28,475
I'm adding the roe.

2491
01:28:28,645 --> 01:28:29,844
It's done.

2492
01:28:29,845 --> 01:28:32,015
- Pastas are ready.
- Thank you.

2493
01:28:32,445 --> 01:28:35,285
(While the pastas are served,)

2494
01:28:37,885 --> 01:28:40,755
(the original tteokbokki has finally simmered down.)

2495
01:28:41,325 --> 01:28:44,495
(It's getting ready to be served quickly.)

2496
01:28:45,995 --> 01:28:47,824
It's done. The medium one is ready.

2497
01:28:47,825 --> 01:28:48,864
Okay.

2498
01:28:48,865 --> 01:28:50,094
- I'll carry it.
- Okay.

2499
01:28:50,095 --> 01:28:51,535
- This is the one, right?
- Yes, it is.

2500
01:28:51,795 --> 01:28:52,904
- Thank you.
- Sure.

2501
01:28:52,905 --> 01:28:54,634
(It's served right away.)

2502
01:28:54,635 --> 01:28:55,675
Goodness.

2503
01:28:55,905 --> 01:28:57,305
It's hard to run a business, isn't it?

2504
01:28:57,975 --> 01:28:58,975
It's okay.

2505
01:28:58,976 --> 01:29:00,044
(Hitting a nerve)

2506
01:29:00,045 --> 01:29:01,704
Here's your tteokbokki.

2507
01:29:01,705 --> 01:29:02,714
Okay.

2508
01:29:02,715 --> 01:29:04,374
Please enjoy. Sorry for keeping you waiting.

2509
01:29:04,375 --> 01:29:05,544
- No, it's okay.
- Sorry.

2510
01:29:05,545 --> 01:29:06,584
- Enjoy.
- We talked.

2511
01:29:06,585 --> 01:29:09,155
We talked to the village chief.

2512
01:29:09,815 --> 01:29:12,755
(Unlike what they said, they eat hurriedly.)

2513
01:29:13,355 --> 01:29:14,454
It's tasty, indeed.

2514
01:29:14,455 --> 01:29:15,954
(A tough critic)

2515
01:29:15,955 --> 01:29:18,725
(Remaining order: Original, medium)

2516
01:29:18,995 --> 01:29:20,064
Okay.

2517
01:29:20,065 --> 01:29:21,165
(In the kitchen,)

2518
01:29:21,495 --> 01:29:22,535
It's done.

2519
01:29:23,165 --> 01:29:25,195
(Mimi sets the fritters.)

2520
01:29:25,605 --> 01:29:27,165
Mimi, those are for the original, right?

2521
01:29:27,265 --> 01:29:28,565
- Yes, they are.
- Thank you.

2522
01:29:28,835 --> 01:29:31,835
(Young Ji checks the flavour.)

2523
01:29:32,205 --> 01:29:33,745
(Satisfied)

2524
01:29:33,975 --> 01:29:35,575
The original tastes the best.

2525
01:29:36,145 --> 01:29:37,574
You're so good at frying food.

2526
01:29:37,575 --> 01:29:38,645
- Am I?
- Yes.

2527
01:29:39,045 --> 01:29:40,414
Those fritters are really tasty.

2528
01:29:40,415 --> 01:29:42,384
(The kitchen is a bit relaxed.)

2529
01:29:42,385 --> 01:29:44,084
We have a moment to catch our breath now.

2530
01:29:44,085 --> 01:29:45,385
I'm glad to hear that.

2531
01:29:45,855 --> 01:29:48,355
(Space Rice Cake)

2532
01:29:49,255 --> 01:29:51,855
(They are the ones who said they'd be back.)

2533
01:29:54,495 --> 01:29:55,495
(Three people.)

2534
01:29:55,495 --> 01:29:56,495
(I'm a customer too.)

2535
01:29:56,496 --> 01:29:57,565
Please wait.

2536
01:29:57,965 --> 01:29:59,665
We entered this way.

2537
01:29:59,965 --> 01:30:01,465
I think you can go in through that door.

2538
01:30:01,565 --> 01:30:02,605
It's confusing.

2539
01:30:03,375 --> 01:30:05,335
- Hurry up.
- Go in.

2540
01:30:05,905 --> 01:30:07,305
Welcome.

2541
01:30:08,775 --> 01:30:10,714
- What? You're finally here.
- Hey.

2542
01:30:10,715 --> 01:30:12,544
- Welcome.
- They're here.

2543
01:30:12,545 --> 01:30:13,545
Right.

2544
01:30:13,546 --> 01:30:15,444
- We're done.
- They're good.

2545
01:30:15,445 --> 01:30:16,984
The tables are full now.

2546
01:30:16,985 --> 01:30:18,154
Have a seat. Don't stand like that.

2547
01:30:18,155 --> 01:30:19,455
Hello.

2548
01:30:20,385 --> 01:30:22,155
We'll get the original tteokbokki.

2549
01:30:22,395 --> 01:30:23,924
And the one with the pollack roe.

2550
01:30:23,925 --> 01:30:25,194
- Pollack roe...
- Just order two.

2551
01:30:25,195 --> 01:30:26,524
How about drinks?

2552
01:30:26,525 --> 01:30:27,694
What are the drinks?

2553
01:30:27,695 --> 01:30:28,864
(Smiling to sell some drinks)

2554
01:30:28,865 --> 01:30:30,935
By the way, you're pretty like those idols.

2555
01:30:31,065 --> 01:30:33,165
- Me? I'm an idol.
- She's an idol.

2556
01:30:33,265 --> 01:30:34,464
(You may have forgotten, but Yu Jin's an idol.)

2557
01:30:34,465 --> 01:30:35,504
You're so pretty.

2558
01:30:35,505 --> 01:30:37,534
- Thank you.
- A fancy coffee?

2559
01:30:37,535 --> 01:30:39,505
- That one.
- Coffee? Would you like a coffee?

2560
01:30:39,745 --> 01:30:41,244
- Their pomegranate slushy is good.
- Pomegranate slushy?

2561
01:30:41,245 --> 01:30:42,645
Are you having the pomegranate slushy?

2562
01:30:43,145 --> 01:30:45,475
A new table is here.

2563
01:30:46,645 --> 01:30:47,944
(Head Chef is malfunctioning again.)

2564
01:30:47,945 --> 01:30:50,085
A new table is here.

2565
01:30:50,485 --> 01:30:52,754
- One small original tteokbokki.
- Okay.

2566
01:30:52,755 --> 01:30:54,055
And one pollack roe and clam pasta.

2567
01:30:54,525 --> 01:30:55,585
Got it.

2568
01:30:55,855 --> 01:30:58,155
(The kitchen team looks exhausted.)

2569
01:30:58,395 --> 01:31:00,364
- Everyone said it was tasty.
- I'm glad to hear that.

2570
01:31:00,365 --> 01:31:01,464
Are they new customers?

2571
01:31:01,465 --> 01:31:02,664
- Yes.
- They're new customers.

2572
01:31:02,665 --> 01:31:03,894
How old are they?

2573
01:31:03,895 --> 01:31:06,205
They are the ones who said they'd be back.

2574
01:31:06,735 --> 01:31:09,405
Then I'll show them what I got.

2575
01:31:10,175 --> 01:31:13,175
(In the meantime, Yu Jin serves the slushies.)

2576
01:31:13,345 --> 01:31:14,874
Here are your drinks.

2577
01:31:14,875 --> 01:31:16,144
Here's your coffee.

2578
01:31:16,145 --> 01:31:17,974
Is it possible to make it not sweet?

2579
01:31:17,975 --> 01:31:19,214
Yes, I can go into the container and...

2580
01:31:19,215 --> 01:31:21,384
Would you like to taste it and see how sweet it is?

2581
01:31:21,385 --> 01:31:22,814
Do you want to try it a little?

2582
01:31:22,815 --> 01:31:23,985
Just get me a cup.

2583
01:31:25,855 --> 01:31:27,125
- I'll bring it, Eun Ji.
- Okay.

2584
01:31:27,525 --> 01:31:30,195
(The additional order is served.)

2585
01:31:30,895 --> 01:31:32,054
The service team...

2586
01:31:32,055 --> 01:31:34,065
- is doing a great job.
- Yes.

2587
01:31:34,665 --> 01:31:36,334
(Eun Ji even checks the customers from time to time.)

2588
01:31:36,335 --> 01:31:37,565
Is it too hot for you?

2589
01:31:37,795 --> 01:31:38,964
Is it okay? Anybody feeling hot?

2590
01:31:38,965 --> 01:31:40,035
We can take off our clothes.

2591
01:31:41,835 --> 01:31:44,175
(Right up Eun Ji's alley)

2592
01:31:44,305 --> 01:31:46,505
How many clothes are you going to take off?

2593
01:31:46,805 --> 01:31:47,805
(Laughing)

2594
01:31:47,806 --> 01:31:49,014
That was very spicy.

2595
01:31:49,015 --> 01:31:50,074
No, it's all good.

2596
01:31:50,075 --> 01:31:51,245
That was great.

2597
01:31:51,745 --> 01:31:53,314
- Please enjoy and take your time.
- Okay.

2598
01:31:53,315 --> 01:31:54,785
(The customers are happy thanks to Eun Ji.)

2599
01:31:54,945 --> 01:31:57,215
The original tteokbokki can be served now.

2600
01:31:58,185 --> 01:32:00,254
(While the service team is working their magic,)

2601
01:32:00,255 --> 01:32:02,324
(they finished the dishes.)

2602
01:32:02,325 --> 01:32:04,425
Here's your pollack roe and clam pasta.

2603
01:32:05,295 --> 01:32:06,725
(Tasting)

2604
01:32:06,825 --> 01:32:08,224
The pollack roe dish is tasty.

2605
01:32:08,225 --> 01:32:09,394
It's tasty, isn't it?

2606
01:32:09,395 --> 01:32:11,395
- The rice cakes are good.
- Yes.

2607
01:32:11,665 --> 01:32:13,205
The rice cakes are chewy and tasty.

2608
01:32:13,365 --> 01:32:14,565
(Nodding)

2609
01:32:15,205 --> 01:32:17,205
(He is recommending the place on his phone.)

2610
01:32:17,405 --> 01:32:19,275
It's worth visiting once in a while, isn't it?

2611
01:32:20,205 --> 01:32:22,575
(Space Rice Cake is thriving.)

2612
01:32:22,915 --> 01:32:24,444
I'm glad we're full, Yu Jin.

2613
01:32:24,445 --> 01:32:25,475
I know, Eun Ji.

2614
01:32:26,545 --> 01:32:29,555
(Just as they breathed a sigh of relief...)

2615
01:32:32,355 --> 01:32:33,425
Gosh. Hello.

2616
01:32:33,925 --> 01:32:35,225
- Hello.
- Please come in.

2617
01:32:35,585 --> 01:32:37,224
- How many people?
- My gosh.

2618
01:32:37,225 --> 01:32:38,294
- Two?
- Hello.

2619
01:32:38,295 --> 01:32:39,395
(Arriving at fully booked Space Rice Cake)

2620
01:32:40,095 --> 01:32:41,624
If you could wait a little,

2621
01:32:41,625 --> 01:32:43,735
we'll contact you as soon as a table opens up.

2622
01:32:44,295 --> 01:32:47,365
- We have a waiting list now.
- We do?

2623
01:32:47,665 --> 01:32:49,005
- We have one group waiting.
- One group?

2624
01:32:49,575 --> 01:32:52,705
I'm not used to this kind of fame.

2625
01:32:53,275 --> 01:32:56,015
What? It's not at all what I expected.

2626
01:32:56,275 --> 01:32:58,075
(Epilogue)

2627
01:32:58,345 --> 01:32:59,914
- Well done.
- Well done, everyone.

2628
01:32:59,915 --> 01:33:00,985
Let's go home.

2629
01:33:01,615 --> 01:33:03,914
- Can we go back to Seoul?
- To Seoul?

2630
01:33:03,915 --> 01:33:04,985
- I want to go back to Seoul.
- Straighten your back.

2631
01:33:05,355 --> 01:33:06,425
Do you want to go back to Seoul?

2632
01:33:08,125 --> 01:33:10,055
- I'm scared.
- Goodness.

2633
01:33:10,425 --> 01:33:12,354
You wanted to make rice cakes, so we set up rice cake machines.

2634
01:33:12,355 --> 01:33:14,295
If you want to go back to Seoul, we'll make it happen.

2635
01:33:14,825 --> 01:33:16,394
- Are we going to Seoul, Young Ji?
- But our tteokbokki...

2636
01:33:16,395 --> 01:33:17,434
(Young Ji's joke ends up causing a huge ripple effect.)

2637
01:33:17,435 --> 01:33:18,464
Are we going back to Seoul?

2638
01:33:18,465 --> 01:33:20,965
(Coming soon)

2639
01:33:21,135 --> 01:33:22,905
(On next episode)

2640
01:33:23,175 --> 01:33:25,575
(The morning of Day 2 of business starts.)

2641
01:33:26,145 --> 01:33:27,175
(Let's go for it.)

2642
01:33:28,475 --> 01:33:29,875
(The service team's favourite part of the day)

2643
01:33:30,275 --> 01:33:31,875
(Grocery shopping time)

2644
01:33:32,245 --> 01:33:34,245
(Object 1 of desire: Headband)

2645
01:33:34,785 --> 01:33:36,785
(Object 2 of desire: Arm sleeves)

2646
01:33:37,115 --> 01:33:41,225
(Object 3 of desire: Kitchen tools)

2647
01:33:41,685 --> 01:33:43,595
(At that time)

2648
01:33:43,955 --> 01:33:46,165
(I don't know if you're aware,)

2649
01:33:46,465 --> 01:33:49,065
(but during the last 2 days, the service team spent 300 dollars.)

2650
01:33:49,365 --> 01:33:51,465
(A shocking piece of information comes in.)

2651
01:33:51,965 --> 01:33:54,235
(How much did you spend on groceries today?)

2652
01:33:54,705 --> 01:33:56,535
(The head chef begins her investigation.)

2653
01:33:56,735 --> 01:33:58,105
(For gimbap...)

2654
01:33:58,405 --> 01:33:59,575
(Did you say gimbap?)

2655
01:34:00,375 --> 01:34:02,045
(We need to cut down on our spending.)

2656
01:34:02,245 --> 01:34:04,975
(The head chef becomes sensitive about expenses tied to sales.)

2657
01:34:05,215 --> 01:34:08,415
(Even when deciding what to have for dinner)

2658
01:34:08,945 --> 01:34:10,515
(Let's check the sales first.)

2659
01:34:11,255 --> 01:34:13,585
(The boss's desire to make money is on another level.)

2660
01:34:13,925 --> 01:34:16,395
(She starts connecting everything back to sales.)

2661
01:34:16,925 --> 01:34:18,925
(Young Ji at Space Rice Cake)

2662
01:34:19,295 --> 01:34:21,395
(She's a different person.)

2663
01:34:21,995 --> 01:34:23,795
(A new menu to ease the boss' worries)

2664
01:34:24,135 --> 01:34:26,105
(A meeting of vibrant green broccoli...)

2665
01:34:26,365 --> 01:34:28,105
(and fresh basil)

2666
01:34:28,535 --> 01:34:30,875
(Broccolino Basiliano)

2667
01:34:31,205 --> 01:34:32,775
(A special transformation of the classic tteokbokki)

2668
01:34:33,075 --> 01:34:34,845
(It's also known as basil tteokbokki.)

2669
01:34:35,075 --> 01:34:36,375
(Tasting)

2670
01:34:36,645 --> 01:34:38,675
(Not only approved by the employee)

2671
01:34:39,075 --> 01:34:44,255
(Additional orders of Broccolino Basiliano)

2672
01:34:44,515 --> 01:34:46,525
(It becomes a hit with customers too.)

2673
01:34:46,825 --> 01:34:51,895
(Winning over everyone's taste buds, young and old)

2674
01:34:53,595 --> 01:34:56,935
(The ultimate new menu to escape the deficit is coming soon.)
